\par }\pard\plain \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright \fs20 {\fs24 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Growth:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This potion causes the height and weight of the person consuming it to increase. Garments and other worn and carried gear also grow in size. Each fourth of the liquid consumed causes 6 feet of height growth
\emdash 
in other words, a full potion increases height by 24 feet. Weight increases should be proportional to the change in height. Strength is increased sufficiently to allow bearing armor and weapons commensurate with the increased size, but does not provide 
combat bonuses. Movement increases to that of a giant of approximately equal size.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Healing:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 An entire potion must be consumed in a single round. If this is done, the potion restores 2d4 + 2 hit points of damage (see }{\i\fs24 extra-healing}{\fs24  above).
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Heroism:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This gives the imbiber a temporary increase in levels (hit points, combat ability, and saves) if he has fewer than 10 levels of experience.
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx1440\tx2880\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf6 \tab Number of\tab Additonal\tab 
\par Level of\tab Levels\tab Temporary\tab 
\par Imbiber\tab Bestowed\tab Hit Dice}{\fs24\cf6 \tab 
\par }{\fs24     0\tab     4\tab 4d10\tab 
\par 1st-3rd\tab     3\tab 3d10+1\tab 
\par 4th-6th\tab     2\tab 2d10+2\tab 
\par 7th-9th\tab     1\tab 1d10+3\tab 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 
\par }\pard\plain \s15\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\tab When the potion is quaffed, the individual fights as if he were at the experience level bestowed
 by the magic of the elixir. Damage sustained is taken first from magically gained hit dice and bonus points. This potion can only be used by warriors.
\par }\pard\plain \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright \fs20 {\fs24 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Human Control:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 A }{\i\fs24 potion of human control}{\fs24  allows the imbiber to control up to 32 levels or Hit Dice of humans, humanoids, and demihumans as if a }{\i\fs24 charm person}{\fs24 
 spell had been cast. All creatures are entitled to saving throws vs. spell. Any pluses on Hit Dice are rounded down to the lowest whole die (e.g., 1 + 2 = 1, 2 + 6 = 2, etc.). This potion lasts for 5d6
 rounds. The type of human(s) that can be controlled is randomly determined.
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx1440\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf6 D20 Roll\tab Human/Humanoid Controlled}{\fs24\cf6 \tab 
\par }{\fs24 1-2\tab Dwarves\tab 
\par 3-4\tab Elves/Half-Elves\tab 
\par 5-6\tab Gnomes\tab 
\par 7-8\tab Halflings\tab 
\par 9-10\tab Half-Orcs\tab 
\par 11-16\tab Humans\tab 
\par 17-19\tab Humanoids (gnolls, orcs, goblins, etc.)
\par 20\tab Elves, Half-Elves, and Humans
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Invisibility:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 
This potion confers invisibility similar to the 2nd-level wizard spell of the same name. Actions involving combat cause termination of the invisible state. The individual possessing this potion can quaff a single gulp\emdash 
equal to 1/8 of the contents of the container\emdash to bestow invisibility for 3-6 turns.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Invulnerability:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This potion confers immunity to nonmagical weapons. It also protects against attacks from creatures (not characters) with no magical properties or
 with fewer than 4 Hit Dice. Thus, an 8th-level character without a magical weapon could not harm the imbiber of an invulnerability potion.
\par \tab The potion also improves Armor Class rating by 2 classes and gives a bonus of +2 to the individual on his saving th
rows versus all forms of attack. Its effects are realized only when the entire potion is consumed, and they last for 5d4 rounds. Only warriors can use this potion.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Levitation:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 A }{\i\fs24 levitation}{\fs24  potion enables the consumer to levitate in much the same manner a
s the 2nd-level wizard spell of the same name. The potion allows levitation of the individual only, to a maximum weight of 600 pounds. The consumer can carry another person, as long as their total weight is within this limit.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Longevity:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 The }{\i\fs24 longevity}{\fs24  pot
ion reduces the character's age by 1d12 years, restoring youth and vigor. The entire potion must be consumed to achieve the desired result. It is also useful as a counter to magical or monster-based aging attacks.
\par \tab Each time one drinks a }{\i\fs24 longevity}{\fs24  potion, there is a 1% cumulative chance the effect will be the reverse of what the consumer wants\emdash all age removed by previous drinks will be restored!
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Oil of Acid Resistance:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 When this oil is applied to skin, cloth, or any other material, it confers virtual invulnerability against acid. The oil wears off, but slowly\emdash 
one application lasts for a whole day (1440 rounds). Each time the protected material is exposed to acid, the duration of the oil is reduced by as many rounds as hit points of damage the acid would ha
ve caused to exposed flesh. Thus, if a black dragon breathes for 64 points of acid damage, a person protected by this oil would lose 1 hour and 4 minutes of protection (64 rounds\emdash 32 if a saving throw vs. breath weapon was successful).
\par \tab Each flask contains sufficient oil to protect one man-sized creature (and equipment) for 24 hours; or to protect any combination of creatures and duration between these extremes.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Oil of Disenchantment:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This oil enables the removal of all enchantments and charms placed upon
 living things, and the suppression of such effects on objects. If the oil is rubbed in a creature, all enchantments and charms on it are immediately removed. If rubbed onto objects bearing an enchantment, the magic will be lost for 1d10 + 20 turns. After
 
this time, the oil loses potency and the item regains its enchantment. The oil does not radiate magic once it is applied, and masks the enchantment of whatever it coats, so that an item so coated will not show any enchantment for as long as the oil remain
s effective.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Oil of Elemental Invulnerability:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 
This precious substance gives total invulnerability to one type of normal elemental force on the Prime Material Plane: wind storms, fires, earth slides, floods, and so forth. There is a 10% chance that each s
uch flask will also be effective on the appropriate Elemental plane\emdash 
this allows the protected individual to operate freely and without danger from elemental forces. Attacks by elemental creatures are still effective, but with a -1 penalty per die of damage
. A flask contains enough oil to coat one man-sized creature for eight days or eight individuals for one day. The element protected against is determined randomly.
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx2160\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf6 D4 Roll\tab Element}{\fs24\cf6 \tab 
\par }{\fs24 1\tab Air\tab 
\par 2\tab Earth\tab 
\par 3\tab Fire\tab 
\par 4\tab Water\tab 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Oil of Etherealness:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This potion is act
ually a light oil that is applied externally to clothes and exposed flesh, conferring etherealness. In the ethereal state, the individual can pass through solid objects in any direction\emdash sideways, upward, downward\emdash 
or to different planes. The individual cannot touch non-ethereal objects.
\par \tab The oil takes effect three rounds after application, and it lasts for 4 + 1d4 turns unless removed with a weak acidic solution prior to the expiration of its normal effective duration. It can be applied to objects as well as
 creatures. One potion is sufficient to anoint a normal human and such gear as he typically carries (two or three weapons, garments, armor, shield, and miscellaneous gear). Ethereal individuals are invisible.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Oil of Fiery Burning:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 When this oil is expose
d to air, it immediately bursts into flame, inflicting 5d6 points of damage to any creature directly exposed to the substance (save vs. spell for half damage). If hurled, the flask will always break. Any creature within 10 feet of the point of impact (up 
t
o a maximum of six creatures) will be affected. The oil can, for instance, be used to consume the bodies of as many as six regenerating creatures, such as trolls. If the flask is opened, the creature holding it immediately suffers 1d4 points of damage. Un
less a roll equal to or less than the creature's Dexterity is made on 2d10, the flask cannot be re-stoppered in time to prevent the oil from exploding, with effects as described above.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Oil of Fumbling:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This oil will seem to be of a useful type\emdash }{\i\fs24 acid resistance, slipperiness,}{\fs24  etc.\emdash 
until the wearer is under stress in an actual melee situation. At that point, he has a 50% chance each round to fumble and drop whatever he holds\emdash weapon, shield, spell components, and so forth. Only a thorough bath of some solvent 
(alcohol, etc.) will remove the oil before it wears off.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Oil of Impact:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This oil has beneficial effects on blunt weapons and missiles, both magical and nonmagical. When applied to a blunt weapon such as a club, hammer, or mace, it bestows a +3 bonus to a
ttack rolls and a +6 bonus to damage. The effect lasts 1d4 + 8 rounds per application. One application will treat one weapon.
\par \tab When applied to a blunt missile, such as a hurled hammer, hurled club, sling stone, or bullet, it bestows a +3 bonus to attack ro
lls and a +3 bonus to damage. The effect last until the missile is used once. One application will treat 4-5 sling stones or two larger weapons. A flask of }{\i\fs24 oil of impact}{\fs24  holds 1d3+2 applications.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24 \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Oil of Slipperiness:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 Similar to the }{\i\fs24  oil of etherealness }{\fs24  
described above, this liquid is to be applied externally. This application makes it impossible for the individual to be grabbed, grasped, or hugged by any opponent, or constricted by snakes or tentacles. (Note that a roper could still inflict weakness, bu
t that the monster's tentacles could not entwine the opponent coated with }{\i\fs24  oil of slipperiness}{\fs24 .)
\par \tab In addition, such obstructions as webs, magical or otherwise, will not effect an anointed individual. Bonds such an ropes, manacles, and chains can be slipped 
free. Magical ropes and the like are not effective against this oil. If poured on a floor or on steps, there is a 95% chance that creatures standing on the surface will slip and fall. The oil requires eight hours to wear off normally, or it can be wiped o
ff with an alcohol solution (even wine!).
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Oil of Timelessness:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 When this oil is applied to any matter that was once alive (leather, leaves, paper, wood, dead flesh, etc.), it allows that substance to resist the passage of time. Each year of actual time af
fects the substance as if only a day had passed. The coated object has a +1 bonus on all saving throws. The oil never wears off, although it can be magically removed. One flask contains enough oil to coat eight man-sized objects, or an equivalent area.

\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Philter of Glibness:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This potion enables the imbiber to speak fluently\emdash even tell lies\emdash smoothly, believably, and undetectably. Magical investigation (such as the 4th-level priest spell,}{\i\fs24 
 detect lie}{\fs24 ) will not give the usual results, but will reveal that some minor "stretching of the truth'' might be occurring.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Philter of Love:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This potion causes the individual drinking it to become charmed (see }{\i\fs24 charm}{\fs24 
 spells) with the first creature seen after consuming the draught. The imbiber may actually become enamored if the creature is of similar race and of the opposite sex. Charm effects wear off in 1d4+4 turns, but the enamoring effects last until a }{
\i\fs24 dispel magic}{\fs24  spell is cast upon the individual.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Philter of Persuasiveness:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 When this potion is imbibed the individual becomes more charismatic, gaining a bonus of +5 on reaction dice rolls. The individual is also able to }{\i\fs24 suggest}{\fs24 
 (see the 3rd-level wizard spell, }{\i\fs24 suggestion}{\fs24 ) once per turn to all creatures within 30 yards of him.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Philter of Stammering and Stuttering}{\b\fs24 :}{\fs24  When this liquid is consumed, it will seem to be beneficial\emdash }{\i\fs24 philter of glibness}{\fs24  or }{\i\fs24 persuasiveness,}{\fs24 
 for instance. However, whenever a meaningful utterance must be spoken (the verbal component of a spell, the text of a scroll, negotiation with a monster, etc.), the potion's true effect is revealed\emdash 
nothing can be said properly, and the reactions of all creatures hearing such nonsense will be at a -5 penalty.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Plant Control:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 A }{\i\fs24 plant control}{\fs24 
 potion enables the individual who consumes it to influence the behavior of vegetable life forms. This includes normal plants, fungi, and even molds and shambling mounds\emdash within the parameters of their normal abilities. The
 imbiber can cause the vegetable forms to remain still or silent, move, entwine, etc., according to their limits.
\par \tab Vegetable monsters with Intelligence of 5 or higher are entitled to a saving throw vs. spell. Plants within a 20-foot by 20-foot square can b
e controlled, subject to the limitations set forth above, for 5d4 rounds. Self-destructive control is not directly possible if the plants are intelligent (see }{\i\fs24 charm plants}{\fs24  spell). Control range is 90 yards.
\par 
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Poison:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 A poison potion is simply a highly tox
ic liquid in a potion flask. Typically, poison potions are odorless and can be of any color. Ingestion, introduction of the poison through a break in the skin, or, in some cases, just skin contact, will cause death. Poison can be }{\i\fs24 weak}{\fs24 
 (+4 to +1 bonus to the saving throw), }{\i\fs24 average,}{\fs24  or }{\i\fs24 deadly}{\fs24  (-1 to -4 penalty or greater on the saving throw). Some poison can be so toxic that a }{\i\fs24 neutralize poison}{\fs24 
 spell will simply lower the toxicity level by 40%\emdash say, from a -4 penalty to a +4 bonus to the saving throw vs. poiso
n. The DM selects the strength of poison desired, although most are strength "J'' (see Table 51, Poison Strength). You might wish to allow characters to hurl poison flasks (see Combat, "Grenade-Like Missiles").
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Polymorph Self:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This potion duplicates the effects of the 4th-level wizard spell of the same name.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Rainbow Hues:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This rather syrupy potion must be stored in a metallic container. The imbiber can become any hue or combination of hues desired at will. Any color or combination of colors is possible,
 if the user simply holds the thought in his mind long enough for the hue to be effected. If the potion is quaffed sparingly, a flask will yield up to seven draughts of one hour duration each.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Speed:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 A }{\i\fs24 potion of speed}{\fs24  increases the movement and combat ca
pabilities of the imbiber by 100%. Thus, a movement rate of 9 becomes 18, and a character normally able to attack once per round attacks twice. This does not reduce spellcasting time, however. Use of a }{\i\fs24 speed}{\fs24 
 potion ages the individual by one year. The aging is permanent, but the other effects last for 5d4 rounds.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Super-Heroism:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This potion gives the individual a temporary increase in levels (see }{\i\fs24 heroism}{\fs24  potion) if he has fewer than 13 levels of experience. It is similar to the }{\i\fs24 heroism}{\fs24 
 potion, but more powerful, and its effects last just 5d6 melee rounds:
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s7\keep\keepn\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx1440\tx2880\outlinelevel6\adjustright \b\cf6 {\tab Number of\tab Additonal\tab 
\par }\pard\plain \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx1440\tx2880\adjustright \fs20 {\b\fs24\cf6 Level of\tab Levels\tab Temporary\tab 
\par Consumer\tab Bestowed\tab Hit Dice}{\fs24\cf6 \tab 
\par }{\fs24     0\tab    6\tab 5d10\tab 
\par 1st-3rd\tab    5\tab 4d10+1\tab 
\par 4th-6th\tab    4\tab 3d10+2\tab 
\par 7th-9th\tab    3\tab 2d10+3\tab 
\par 10th-12th\tab    2\tab 1d10+4\tab 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sweet Water:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This liquid is not actually a potion to be drunk (though it tastes good). }{\i\fs24 Sweet water}{\fs24 
 is added to other liquids in order to change them to pure, drinkable water. It will neutralize poison and ruin magical potions (no saving throw). The contents of a single
 container will change up to 100,000 cubic feet of polluted, salt, or alkaline water to fresh water. It will turn up to 1,000 cubic feet of acid into pure water. The effects of the potion are permanent, but the liquid may be contaminated after an initial 
period of 5d4 rounds.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24 \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Treasure Findings}{\b\fs24 :}{\fs24  A }{\i\fs24 potion of treasure finding}{\fs24 
 empowers the drinker with a location sense, so that he can point to the direction of the nearest mass of treasure. The treasure must be within 240 yards, and its mass must equal metal of at least 10,000 copper pieces or 100 gems or any combination.

\par \tab Note that only valuable metals (copper, silver, electrum, gold, platinum, etc.) and gems (and jewelry, of course) are located. The potion won't locate worthless metals or magical items which 
don't contain precious metals or gems. The imbiber of the potion can "feel'' the direction in which the treasure lies, but not its distance.
\par \tab Intervening substances other than special magical wards or lead-lined walls will not withstand the powers that the liquor bestows upon the individual. The effects of the potion last for 5d4 rounds. (Clever players will attempt triangulation.)
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Undead Control:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This potion in effect gives the imbiber the ability to charm certain ghasts, ghosts, ghouls, shadows, skeleto
ns, spectres, wights, wraiths, vampires, and zombies. The charm ability is similar to the 1st-level wizard spell, }{\i\fs24 charm person.}{\fs24 
 It affects a maximum of 16 Hit Dice of undead, rounding down any hit point additions to the lowest die (e.g., 4 + 1 equals 4 Hit
 Dice). The undead are entitled to saving throws vs. spell only if they have intelligence. Saving throws are rolled with -2 penalties due to the power of the potion; the effects wear off in 5d4 rounds. To determine the type of undead affected by a particu
lar potion, roll 1d10 and consult the following table:
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx1440\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf6 D10 Roll\tab Undead Type}{\fs24\cf6 \tab 
\par }{\fs24  1\tab Ghasts\tab 
\par  2\tab Ghosts\tab 
\par  3\tab Ghouls\tab 
\par  4\tab Shadows\tab 
\par  5\tab Skeletons\tab 
\par  6\tab Spectres\tab 
\par  7\tab Wights\tab 
\par  8\tab Wraiths\tab 
\par  9\tab Vampires\tab 
\par 10\tab Zombies\tab 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Ventriloquism:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This allows the user to make his voice sound as if it (or someone's voice or a similar sound) were issuing from someplace other than where he is\emdash 
from another creature, a statue, from behind a door, down a passage, etc. The user can speak in any language he knows, or make any sound he can normally 
make. To detect the ruse, listeners must roll a successful saving throw vs. spell with a penalty of -2. If cast in conjunction with other illusions, the DM may rule greater penalties or disallow an independent saving throw against this effect\emdash 
the combined illusion may be perfect! The imbiber can use the }{\i\fs24 ventriloquism}{\fs24  ability up to six times within the duration of the potion.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Vitality:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This potion restores the user to full vitality despite exertion, lack of sleep, and going without food and drink for up to
 seven days. It will nullify up to seven days of deprivation, and will continue in effect for the remainder of its seven-day duration. The potion also makes the user proof against poison and disease while it is in effect, and the user will recover lost hi
t points at the rate of 1 every 4 hours.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Water Breathing:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 It is 75% likely that a }{\i\fs24 water breathing}{\fs24  potion will contain t
wo doses, 25% probable that there will be four in the container. The potion allows the character drinking it to breathe normally in liquids that contain suspended oxygen. This ability lasts for one full hour per dose of potion quaffed, with an additional 
1d10 rounds (minutes) variable. Thus, a character who has consumed a water breathing potion could enter the depths of a river, lake, or even the ocean and not drown while the magical effects of the potion persisted.
\par 
\par 
\par }{\fs36\cf12 Scrolls}{\fs24 
\par 
\par \tab Scrolls are generally found in cylinders\emdash 
tubes of ivory, jade, leather, metal, or wood. Some tubes are inscribed with magic runes or writing PCs must read in order to open the container. This is up to the DM. Taking this approach encourages players to select and use }{\i\fs24 read magic}{\fs24 
 or }{\i\fs24 comprehend language}{\fs24  spells. It also makes it possible to protect power scrolls with traps (}{\i\fs24 symbols, explosive runes}{\fs24 ) and }{\i\fs24 curses.}{\fs24 
\par \tab Each scroll is written in its own magical cypher. To understand what type of scroll has been found, the ability to }{\i\fs24 read magic}{\fs24  must be available. Once a scroll is read to determine its contents, a }{\i\fs24 read magic}{\fs24 
 spell is not needed at a subsequent time to invoke its magic. Even a scroll map will appear unreadable until the proper spell (}{\i\fs24 comprehend languages}{\fs24 ) is used.
\par \tab Reading a scroll to find its contents does not invoke its magic unless it is a specially triggered }{\i\fs24 curse.}{\fs24  A }{\i\fs24 cursed}{\fs24 
 scroll can appear to be a scroll of any sort. It radiates no evil or special aura beyond being magical.
\par \tab A }{\i\fs24 protection}{\fs24  scroll can be read by any class of character even without a }{\i\fs24 read magic}{\fs24  spell.
\par \tab If a scroll isn't immediately read to determine its contents, there is a 5% to 30% chance it will fade. The DM sets the percentage or rolls 1d6 to determine it for each scroll.
\par \tab When a spell scroll is examined, the following table can be used to find its nature:
