\par * Several small items, such as magical arrows or bolts together in one container, will be drained simultaneously.
\par 
\par \tab To find ou
t if the draining can be prevented, a d20 roll must be made for the target item. If the die roll result in a number equal to or higher than the number listed on the table above, the target is unaffected. If the roll is lower, the item is drained. Upon dra
ining an item, the rod itself becomes brittle and cannot be used again. Drained items are not restorable, even by }{\i\fs24 wish.}{\fs24 
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Rod of Flailing:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This magical weapon radiates faintly of alteration magic when subjected to a }{\i\fs24 detect magic}{\fs24  spell. Upon the command of i
ts possessor, the weapon activates, changing from a normal-seeming rod to a double-headed flail. In close quarters, or if the wielder is mounted, it is the small, horseman's weapon (base damage 1d4+1, S-M/L); otherwise, it is a footman's weapon (base dama
ge 1d6+1/2d4, S-M/L).
\par \tab In either form, the weapon has a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls. Each of the weapon's two heads can be used to attack, so double hits can be scored, either on a single opponent or on two opponents who are man-sized or smaller and
 standing side by side.
\par \tab If the holder of the rod expends one charge, he gains +4 bonuses on Armor Class and saving throws for one turn. The rod need not be in weapon-form for this protection benefit to be employed. Transforming it into a weapon (or back i
nto a rod) does not expend any charges.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Rod of Lordly Might:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This rod has functions that are spell-like, but it can also be used as magic weapons of various sorts. It also has several more mundane uses. The }{\i\fs24 rod of lordly might}{\fs24 
 is metal, thicker than other rods, with a flanged ball at one end and various studs along its length. It weighs 10 pounds, thus requiring 16 or greater Strength to wield properly (-1 penalty to attack rolls for each point of Strength below 16).
\par 
\par \tab \tab The spell-like functions of the rod are:
\par }{\b\fs24 \bullet  }{\i\fs24 Paralyzation}{\fs24  upon touch, if the wielder so commands
\par }{\b\fs24 \bullet  }{\i\fs24 Fear}{\fs24  upon all enemies viewing it, if the wielder so desires (6-foot maximum range)
\par }{\b\fs24 \bullet  }{\i\fs24 Drain}{\fs24  2d4 hit points from a touched opponent and bestow them upon the rod wielder, 
\par   up to the rod wielder's normal maximum.
\par \tab 
\par \tab Each function draws off one charge from the rod. The functions entitle victims to saving throws vs. spell, with the exception of the draining function above\emdash this requires a successful hit during melee combat.
\par 
\par The weapon uses of the rod do not use charges. These are:
\par }{\b\fs24 
\par \bullet  }{\i\fs24 mace}{\fs24  +2
\par }{\b\fs24 \bullet  }{\i\fs24 sword of flame +1}{\fs24  when button #1 is pushed. A blade springs from the ball; the ball 
\par    becomes the sword's hilt. The weapon shortens to an overall length to three feet.
\par }{\b\fs24 \bullet  }{\i\fs24 battle axe +4}{\fs24  when button #2 is pushed. The sword blade springs forth, and the handle 
\par    can be lengthened up to 12 feet, for an overall length of from 6 feet to 15 feet. In 15-
\par    foot length, the rod is suitable for use as a lance.
\par 
\par The mundane uses of the rod do not use charges. These are:
\par }{\b\fs24 
\par \bullet  }{\fs24 Climbing pole. When button #4 is pushed, a spike that can anchor in granite is extruded 
\par \tab from the ball, while the other end sprouts three sharp hooks. The rod lengthens 5 to 50 
\par \tab feet in a single round, stopping when button #4 is pushed. Horizontal bars three inches 
\par \tab long fold out from the sides, one foot apart, in staggered progression. The rod is firmly 
\par \tab held by spike and hooks and will bear up to 4,000 pounds weight. It retracts by pushing 
\par \tab button #5.
\par }{\b\fs24 \bullet  }{\fs24 The ladder function can also be used to force open doors. The rod's base is planted 30 
\par \tab feet or less from the portal to be forced and is in line with it. The force exerted is equal 
\par \tab to storm giant Strength.
\par }{\b\fs24 \bullet  }{\fs24 When button #6 is pushed, the rod will indicate magnetic north and give the possessor a 
\par \tab knowledge of his approximate depth beneath the surface (or height above it).
\par 
\par \tab The }{\i\fs24 rod of lordly might}{\fs24  cannot be recharged. When its charges are exhausted, spell-like functions cease, as do all weapon functions except the }{\i\fs24 mace +2.}{\fs24  The rod continues to work in all other ways.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24\cf6 \tab Rod of Passage:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This potent item allows its wielder to perform any of the following, one at a time, one per round: }{\i\fs24 astral travel, dimension door, passwall, phase door,}{\fs24  and }{\i\fs24 
teleport without error.}{\fs24  It is necessary to expend one charge to activate the rod, but once it is activated the possessor can perform each of the listed functions one time. The rod remains charged for o
ne day, or until each of the five functions is used. None of the functions can be used a second time unless another charge is expended, whereupon all five of the functions again become available.
\par \tab With respect to }{\i\fs24 astral travel,}{\fs24  the wielder can elect to use
 the rod on as many as five creatures (one of which must be the wielder himself). Each creature then takes on astral form and can travel in that form. Any remaining functions of the rod are cancelled by this action. The rod travels into the Astral plane a
long with the wielder and the other affected creatures, and cannot be used or reactivated until it is returned from the Astral plane.
\par \tab This five-in-one effect doesn't work with respect to the rod's other powers; only }{\i\fs24 astral travel}{\fs24  can be used more than once per activation, and only in the manner described above.
\par \tab The rod exudes a magical aura of the alteration and evocation sort. Because the physical bodies of the travelers, and their possessions, are actually empowered to become astral, the recharging of the rod requires a wizard of 20th level or higher.

\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Rod of Resurrection:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This rod enables a cleric to resurrect the dead\emdash even elven, dwarven, gnome, or halfling\emdash as if he were of high enough level to cast the }{\i\fs24 resurrection}{\fs24 
 spell. No rest is required, as the rod bestows the life giving effects.
\par \tab The rod can be used once per day. The number of charges used to resurrect a character depends on class and race. Total the number of charges indicated for the character's class and race:
