\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Bowl Commanding Water Elementals:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 
This large container is usually fashioned from blue or green semi-precious stone (malachite or lapis lazuli, for example, or sometimes jade). It is about one foot in diameter, half that deep, and relatively fragile. When the bowl is filled with fresh o
r salt water, and certain words are spoken, a water elemental of 12 Hit Dice will appear. The summoning words require one round to speak.
\par \tab Note that if salt water is used, the elemental will be stronger (+2 per Hit Die, maximum 8 hp per die, however). Information about water elementals can be found in the }{\i\fs24 Monstrous Compendium.}{\fs24  (See also }{\i\fs24 bowl of watery death}{
\fs24  below.)
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Bowl of Watery Death:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This device looks exactly like a }{\i\fs24 bowl commanding water elementals,}{\fs24  right down to the color, design, magical radiation, e
tc. However, when it is filled with water, the wizard must successfully save vs. spell or be shrunk to the size of a small ant and plunged into the center of the bowl. If salt water is poured into the bowl, the saving throw suffers a -2 penalty.
\par \tab The victim will drown in 1d6 + 2 rounds, unless magic is used to save him, for he cannot be physically removed from the }{\i\fs24 bowl of watery death}{\fs24  except by magical means: }{\i\fs24 animal growth, enlarge,}{\fs24  or }{\i\fs24 wish}{
\fs24  are the only spells that will free the victim and restore normal size; a }{\i\fs24 potion of growth}{\fs24  poured into the water will have the same effect; a }{\i\fs24 sweet water}{\fs24 
 potion will grant the victim another saving throw (i.e., a chance that the curse magic of the bowl works only briefly). If the victim drowns, death is permanent, no resurrection is possible, and even a }{\i\fs24 wish}{\fs24  will not work.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Bracers of Archery:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 These magical wrist bands are indistinguishable from normal, non-magical protective wear. When worn by a character type or creature able to employ a bow, they enable the wearer to ex
cel at archery.
\par \tab The bracers empower such a wearer to use any bow (not including crossbows) as if he were proficient in its usage, if such
 is not already the case. If the wearer of the bracers has proficiency with any type of bow, he gains a +2 bonus to attack rolls and a +1 bonus to damage inflicted whenever that type of bow is used. These bonuses are cumulative with any others, including 
those already bestowed by a magical bow or magical arrows, except for a bonus due to weapon specialization.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Bracers of Brachiation:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 These wrist bands appear to be of the ordinary sort, but they enable the wearer to move by swinging from one tree limb, vin
e, etc., to another to get from place to place. The power can be employed only in locales where these sorts of hand-holds can be found. Movement is at a rate of 3, 6, or 9\emdash the more jungle-like the conditions, the greater the movement rate.
\par \tab The wearer is also able to climb trees, vines, poles, ropes, etc., at a rate of 6, and can swing on a rope, vine, or other dangling, flexible object as if he were an ape.
\par \tab The wearer can also jump as if wearing }{\i\fs24 boots of striding and springing,}{\fs24  but the jump must culminate
 in the grasping of a rope or vine, movement through the upper portion of trees, the climbing of a tree or pole, or some other activity associated with brachiation.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Bracers of Defense:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 These items appear to be wrist or arm guards. Their magic bestows an 
effective Armor Class equal to someone wearing armor and employing a shield. If armor is actually worn, the bracers have no additional effect, but they do work in conjunction with other magical items of protection. The Armor Class the }{\i\fs24 
bracers of defense}{\fs24  bestow is determined by making a percentile roll and consulting the table below:
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx1440\tx2160\tx8280\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf6 D100 Roll\tab    Armor Class}{\fs24\cf6 \tab 
\par }{\fs24 01-05\tab \tab 8\tab 
\par 06-15\tab \tab 7\tab 
\par 16-35\tab \tab 6\tab 
\par 36-50\tab \tab 5\tab 
\par 51-70\tab \tab 4\tab 
\par 71-85\tab \tab 3\tab 
\par 86-00\tab \tab 2\tab 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Bracers of Defenselessness:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 These appear to be }{\i\fs24 bracers of defense,}{\fs24  and will ac
tually serve as such until the wearer is attacked in anger by a dangerous enemy. At that moment, the bracers worsen Armor Class to 10 and negate any and all other magical protections and Dexterity bonuses. }{\i\fs24 Bracers of defenselessness}{\fs24 
 can be removed only by means of a }{\i\fs24 remove curse}{\fs24  spell.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Brazier Commanding Fire Elementals:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 
This device appears to be a normal container for holding burning coals unless magic is detected for. It enables a mage to summon an elemental of 12-Hit-Dice strength from the Elemental Plane of Fire. A fire must be lit in the brazier\emdash 
one round is required to do so. If sulphur is added, the elemental will gain +1 on each Hit Die (i.e., 2-9 hit points per Hit Die). The fire elemental will appear as soon as the fire is burning and a command word is uttered. (See }{\i\fs24 
Monstrous Compendium}{\fs24  for other details.)
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Brazier of Sleep Smoke:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This device is exactly like the }{\i\fs24 brazier commanding fire elementals.}{\fs24  However, when a fire is started within it, the burning causes a great cloud of magical smoke to pour
 forth in a 10-foot radius from the brazier. All creatures within the cloud must successfully save vs. spell or fall into a deep sleep.
\par \tab At the same moment, a fire elemental of 12 Hit Dice appears and attacks the nearest creature. Sleeping creatures can be awakened only by means of a }{\i\fs24 dispel magic}{\fs24  or }{\i\fs24 remove curse}{\fs24  spell.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Brooch of Shielding:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This appears to be a piece of silver or gold jewelry (10% chance that there are jewels set in it). It is used to fasten a cloak or cape. In addition to this mundane tas
k, it can absorb magic missiles of the sort generated by spell, wand, or other magical device. A brooch can absorb up to 101 points of }{\i\fs24 magic missile}{\fs24 
 damage before it melts and becomes useless. Its use can be determined only by means of a }{\i\fs24 detect magic}{\fs24  spell and then experimentation.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Broom of Animated Attack:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This is indistinguishable from a normal broom, except by means of detection of its magic. It is identical to a }{\i\fs24 broom of flying}{\fs24 
 by all tests short of attempted use. Using it reveals that a }{\i\fs24 broom of animated attack}{\fs24  is a very nasty item:
\par \tab If a command word ("fly,'' "soar,'' etc.) is spoken, the broom will do a loop-the-loop with its hopeful rider, dumping him on his head from 1d4 + 5 feet off the ground. The broom will then attack the stunned victim, swatt
ing the face with the straw/twig end to blind and beating with the handle end.
\par \tab The broom gets two attacks per round with each end (two swats with the straw, two with the handle). It attacks as if it were a 4-Hit-Dice monster. The straw end causes blindnes
s for one round if it hits. The other end causes 1d3 points of damage when it hits. The broom is Armor Class 7 and takes 18 hit points to destroy.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Broom of Flying:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This magical broom is able to fly through the air at up to 30 base movement speed. The bro
om can carry 182 pounds at this rate, but every 14 additional pounds slows movement by 1. The device can climb or dive at an angle of 30 degrees. A command word (determined by the DM) must be used. The broom will travel alone to any destination named. It 
will come to its owner from as far away as 300 yards when he speaks the command word.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Bucknard's Everfall Purse:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This item appears to be a leather pouch or small bag. Each morning it duplicates certain coins\emdash and possibly gems as well. When found, the purs
e will be full of coins. If totally emptied, and left so for more than a few minutes, the magic of the purse is lost, but if one of any coin is placed within the bag, many coins of the same type will be found inside the next morning. The types of coins fo
und is determined by consulting the table below.
\par \tab Once the type of bag is determined by roll, its abilities will not change.
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf6 D100 }{\fs24\cf6 
