\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 
\par * Base 10 gp gems that can increase to a maximum of 100 gp only.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Candle of Invocation:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 These specially blessed tapers are dedicated to the pantheon of gods of one of the nine alignments. The typical candle is not remarkable, but if a }{\i\fs24 detection}{\fs24 
 spell is cast, it will radiate magic. It also radiates good or evil, if appropriate.
\par \tab Simply burning the candle generates a favorable aura for the individual so doing\emdash if the candle's alignment matches that of the character's. If burned by a priest of the same alignment, the candle temporarily 
increases the priest's level of experience by 2, enabling him to cast additional spells. He can even cast spells normally unavailable to him, as if he were of the higher level, but only so long as the candle continues to burn. Any burning allows the casti
ng of a }{\i\fs24 gate}{\fs24  spell, the respondent being of the alignment of the candle, but the taper is immediately consumed in the process.
\par \tab Otherwise, each candle burns for four hours. It is possible to extinguish the candle as placed in a lantern or otherwise sheltered to protect it from drafts and other things which could put it out. This doesn't affect its magical properties.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Carpet of Flying:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 The size, carrying capacity, and speed of a carpet are determined by rolling percentile dice and consulting the table below
. Each carpet has its own command word (if you use the optional command word rules) to activate it\emdash if the device is within voice range, the command word will activate it. The carpet is then controlled by spoken directions.
\par \tab These rugs are of oriental make and design. Each is beautiful and durable. Note, however, that tears or other rents cannot be repaired without special weaving techniques generally known only in distant, exotic lands.
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx1260\tx2340\tx3960\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf6 D100\tab 
\par Roll\tab Size\tab Capacity\tab Speed}{\fs24\cf6 \tab 
\par }{\fs24 01-20\tab 3' x 5'\tab 1 person\tab   42\tab 
\par 21-55\tab 4' x 6'\tab 2 people\tab   36\tab 
\par 56-80\tab 5' x 7'\tab 3 people\tab   30\tab 
\par 81-00\tab 6' x 9'\tab 4 people\tab   24\tab 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Censer Controlling Air Elementals:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This 6-inch wide, 1-inch high perforated golden vessel resembles thuribles found in places of worship. If filled with incense and lit, a c
ommand word need only be spoken to summon forth a 12 Hit Dice air elemental on the following round. If }{\i\fs24 incense of meditation}{\fs24 
 is burned within the censer, the air elemental will have a +3 bonus to each of its Hit Dice, and it will obey the commands of its summoner. If the censer is extinguished, the elemental will remain and turn on the summoner (see Elemental in the }{\i\fs24 
Monstrous Compendium}{\fs24 ).
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Censer of Summoning Hostile Air Elementals:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This thurible is indistinguishable from other magical and ordinary censers
. It is cursed: any incense burned within it causes 1d4 enraged air elementals to appear, one per round. These attack any and all creatures within sight. The censer cannot be extinguished, and it will burn until either the summoner or the elementals have 
been killed.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Chime of Hunger:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This device looks exactly like a }{\i\fs24 chime of opening.}{\fs24  In fact, it will operate as a }{\i\fs24 chime of opening}{\fs24  for several uses before its curse is put into operation.
\par \tab When the curse takes effect, at the DM's discretion, striking the chi
me causes all creatures within 60 feet to be immediately struck with ravenous hunger. Characters will tear into their rations, ignoring everything else, even dropping everything they are holding in order to eat. Creatures without food immediately availabl
e will rush to where the }{\i\fs24 chime of hunger}{\fs24  sounded and attack any creatures there in order to kill and eat them.
\par \tab All creatures must eat for at least one round. After that, they are entitled to a saving throw vs. spell on each successive round until they succeed. At that point, hunger is satisfied.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Chime of Interruption:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This magical instrument can be struck once per turn. Its resonant tone lasts for three full rounds. While the chime is resonating, no spell requiring a verbal component can be cast within a 
30-foot radius of it unless the caster is able to make a saving throw vs. breath weapon. After its effects fade, the chime must be rested for at least seven rounds. If it is struck again before this time elapses, no sound issues forth, and a full turn mus
t elapse from that point in time before it can again be sounded.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Chime of Opening:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 A }{\i\fs24 chime of opening}{\fs24  is a hollow mithral tube about 1 foot long. When it is struck, it sends forth magical vibrations that cause locks, lids, doors, valves, and portals to op
en. The device functions against normal bars, shackles, chains, bolts, etc. The }{\i\fs24 chime of opening}{\fs24  also destroys the magic of a }{\i\fs24 hold portal}{\fs24  spell or even a }{\i\fs24 wizard lock}{\fs24 
 cast by a wizard of less than 15th level.
\par \tab The chime must be pointed at the area of the it
em or gate which is to be loosed or opened. It is then struck, a clear chiming ring sounds (which may attract monsters), and in one round the target lock is unlocked, the shackle is loosed, the secret door is opened, or the lid of the chest is lifted. If 
a chest is chained, padlocked, locked, and }{\i\fs24 wizard locked,}{\fs24  it will take four soundings of the chime of opening to get it open. A }{\i\fs24 silence}{\fs24 
 spell negates the power of the device. The chime has 1d8 x 10 charges before it cracks and becomes useless.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Cloak of Arachnida:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This black garment gives the wearer the ability to climb as if a }{\i\fs24 spider climb}{\fs24 
 spell had been placed upon him. When magic is detected for, the cloak radiates a strong aura of alteration magic.
\par \tab In addition to the wall-climbing ability, the cloak grants the wearer immunity to entrapment by webs of any sort\emdash 
the wearer can actually move in webs at a rate equal to that of the spider that created the web, or at a base movement rate of 6 in other cases.
\par \tab Once per day the wearer of this cloak can cast a double-sized }{\i\fs24 web.}{\fs24  This operates like the 2nd-level wizard spell.
\par \tab Finally, the wearer is less subject to the poison of arachnids. He gains a +2 bonus to all saving throws vs. such poison.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Cloak of the Bat:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 Fashioned of dark brown or black cloth, a cloak of
 this type is not readily noticeable as unusual. It radiates both enchantment and alteration in equal proportions. The cloak bestows a 90% probability of being invisible when the wearer is stationary within a shadowy or dark place. The wearer is also able
 to hang upside down from the ceiling, like a bat, and to maintain this same chance of invisibility.
\par \tab By holding the edges of the garment, the wearer is able to fly at a speed of 15 (Maneuver Class: B). If he desires, the wearer can actually transform himself into an ordinary bat\emdash 
all possessions worn or carried will be part of the transformation\emdash and fly accordingly. Flying, either with the cloak or as an ordinary bat, can be accomplished only in darkness (either under the night sky or in a lightless or near-
lightless environment underground). Either of the flying powers is usable for up to one hour at a time, but after a flight of any duration, the cloak will not bestow any flying power for a like period of time.
\par \tab The cloak also provides a +2 bonus to Armor Class. This benefit extends to the wearer even when he is in bat form.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Cloak of Displacement:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This item appe
ars to be a normal cloak, but when it is worn by a character its magical properties distort and warp light waves. This displacement of light wave causes the wearer to appear to be 1 foot to 2 feet from his actual position. Any missile or melee attack aime
d at the wearer automatically misses the first time. This can apply to first attacks from multiple opponents only if the second and successive attackers were unable to observe the initial displacement miss.
\par \tab After the first attack, the cloak affords a +2 bo
nus to protection (i.e., two classes better on Armor Class), as well as a +2 bonus to saving throws versus attacks directed at the wearer (such as spells, gaze weapon attacks, spitting and breath attacks, etc., which are aimed at the wearer of the }{
\i\fs24 cloak of displacement}{\fs24 ).
\par \tab Note that 75% of all }{\i\fs24 cloaks of displacement}{\fs24  are sized for humans or elves (persons 5 to 6 feet tall), and 25% are sized for persons of about 4 feet in height (dwarves, gnomes, halflings).
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Cloak of Elvenkind:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This cloak of neutral gray cl
oth is indistinguishable from an ordinary cloak of the same color. However, when it is worn, with the hood drawn up around the head, it enables the wearer to be nearly invisible\emdash the cloak has chameleon-like powers.
\par \tab Outdoors, in natural surroundings, the w
earer of the cloak is almost totally invisible; in other settings, he is nearly so. However, the wearer is easily seen if violently or hastily moving, regardless of the surroundings. The invisibility bestowed is:
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx180\tx2700\adjustright {\fs24 \tab }{\i\fs24 Outdoors, natural surroundings}{\fs24 
\par \tab heavy growth\tab 100%
\par \tab light growth\tab  99%
\par \tab open fields\tab  95%
\par \tab rocky terrain\tab  98%
\par 
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Urban surroundings}{\fs24 
\par \tab buildings\tab  90%
\par \tab brightly lit room\tab  50%
\par 
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Underground}{\fs24 
\par \tab torch/lantern light\tab  95%
\par \tab infravision\tab  90%
\par \tab light/continual light\tab  50%
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab Fully 90% of these cloaks are sized for human or elven-sized persons. The other 10% are sized for smaller persons (4 feet or so in height).
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Cloak of the Manta Ray:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This cloak appears to be made of leather until the wearer enters salt water. At that time the }{\i\fs24 cloak of the manta ray}{\fs24  adheres to the
 individual, and he appears nearly identical to a manta-ray\emdash there is only a 10% chance that someone seeing the wearer will know he isn't a manta ray.
\par \tab The wearer can breathe underwater and has a movement rate of 18, like a manta ray (see the }{\i\fs24 Monstrous Compendium}{\fs24 
). The wearer also has an Armor Class of at least six, that of a manta ray. Other magical protections or magical armor can improve that armor value.
\par \tab 
Although the cloak does not enable the wearer to bite opponents as a manta ray does, the garment has a tail spine which can be used to strike at opponents behind him. The spine inflicts 1d6 points of damage, and there is no chance of stunning. This attack
 can be used in addition to other sorts, for the wearer can release his arms from the cloak without sacrificing underwater movement if so desired.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Cloak of Poisonousness:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This particular cloak is usually made of a wool-like material, although it can be ma
de of leather. It radiates magic. The cloak can be handled without harm, but as soon as it is actually donned, the wearer is stricken stone dead.
\par \tab A }{\i\fs24 cloak of poisonousness}{\fs24  can be removed only with a }{\i\fs24 remove curse}{\fs24  spell\emdash this destroys the magical properties of the cloak. If a }{\i\fs24 neutralize poison}{\fs24 
 spell is then used, it may be possible to revive the victim with a }{\i\fs24 raise dead}{\fs24  or }{\i\fs24 resurrection}{\fs24  spell, but there is a -10% chance of success because of the poison.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Cloak of Protection:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 The various forms of this marvelous device all appear to be normal garments made of cloth or leather. However, each plus of a }{\i\fs24 cloak of protection}{\fs24 
 betters Armor Class by one and adds one to saving throw die rolls. Thus, a }{\i\fs24 cloak +1}{\fs24  would lower Armor Class
 10 (no armor) to Armor Class 9, and give a +1 bonus to saving throw rolls. To determine how powerful a given cloak is, roll percentile dice and consult the table below:
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx1080\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf6 D100
\par Roll\tab Power}{\fs24\cf6 \tab 
\par }{\fs24 01-35\tab cloak +1\tab 
\par 36-65\tab cloak +2\tab 
\par 66-85\tab cloak +3\tab 
\par 86-95\tab cloak +4\tab 
\par 96-00\tab cloak +5\tab 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This device can be combined with other items or worn with leather armor. It cannot function in conjunction with any sort of magical armor, normal armor not made of leather, or with a shield of any sort.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Crystal Ball:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This is the most common
 form of scrying device: a crystal sphere about 6 inches in diameter. A wizard can use the device to see over virtually any distance or into other planes of existence. The user of a }{\i\fs24 crystal ball}{\fs24 
 must know the subject to be viewed. Knowledge can be from personal acquaintance, possession of personal belongings, a likeness of the object, or accumulated information. Knowledge, rather than distance, is the key to how successful location will be:

\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx2880\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf6 \tab Chance of\tab 
\par Subject is\tab Locating*}{\fs24\cf6 \tab 
\par }{\fs24 Personally well known\tab 100%\tab 
\par Personally known slightly\tab   85%\tab 
\par Pictured\tab   50%\tab 
\par Part of in possession\tab   50%\tab 
\par Garment in possession\tab   25%\tab 
\par Well informed of\tab   25%\tab 
\par Slightly informed of\tab   20%\tab 
\par On another plane\tab -25%\tab 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 * Unless masked by magic.
\par 
\par \tab The chance of locating also dictates how long and how frequently a wizard will be able to view the subject.
\par 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx1800\tx3240\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf6 Chances of\tab Viewing\tab 
\par Locating*\tab Period\tab Frequency}{\fs24\cf6 \tab 
\par }{\fs24 100% or more\tab 1 hour\tab 3 times/day\tab 
\par 99% to 90%\tab 30 minutes\tab 3 times/day\tab 
\par 89% to 75%\tab 30 minutes\tab 2 times/day\tab 
\par 74% to 50%\tab 30 minutes\tab 1 time/day\tab 
\par 49% to 25%\tab 15 minutes\tab 1 time/day\tab 
\par 24% or less\tab 10 minutes\tab 1 time/day\tab 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 * Unless masked by magic.
\par 
\par \tab Viewing beyond the periods or frequencies noted will force the wizard to roll a saving throw vs. spell each round. A failed saving throw permanently lowers the character's Intelligence by one point and drives him insane until healed.
\par \tab Certain spells cast upon the user of the }{\i\fs24 crystal ball}{\fs24  can improve his chances of using the device successfully. These are }{\i\fs24 comprehend languages, read magic, infravision,}{\fs24  and }{\i\fs24 tongues.}{\fs24  Two spells
\emdash }{\i\fs24 detect magic}{\fs24  and }{\i\fs24 detect evil/good}{\fs24 \emdash can be cast through a }{\i\fs24 crystal ball.}{\fs24  The chance of success is 5% per level of experience of the wizard.
\par \tab Certain }{\i\fs24 crystal balls}{\fs24  have additional powers. These spell functions operate at 10th level. To determine whether a }{\i\fs24 crystal ball}{\fs24  has extra powers, roll percentile dice and consult the table below:
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx1440\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf6 D100
\par Roll\tab Additional Power}{\fs24\cf6 \tab 
\par }{\fs24 01-50\tab }{\i\fs24 crystal ball}{\fs24 \tab 
\par 51-75\tab }{\i\fs24 crystal ball}{\fs24  with }{\i\fs24 clairaudience}{\fs24 \tab 
\par 76-90\tab }{\i\fs24 crystal ball}{\fs24  with }{\i\fs24 ESP}{\fs24 \tab 
\par 91-00\tab }{\i\fs24 crystal ball}{\fs24  with }{\i\fs24 telepathy}{\fs24 *\tab  
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 *Communication only.
\par 
\par \tab Only creatures with Intelligence of 12 or better have a chance of noticing that they are the subjects of scrying. The base chance is determined by class.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s1\keep\keepn\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx1620\outlinelevel0\adjustright {Fighter\tab 2%
\par }\pard\plain \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx1620\adjustright \fs20 {\fs24 Paladin\tab 6%
\par Ranger\tab 4%
\par Bard\tab 3%
\par Thief\tab 6%
\par Spell-User\tab 8%
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab For each point of Intelligence above 12, the creature has an additional arithmetically ascending cumulative chance beginning at 1% (i.e., 1% at Intelligence 13, 3% at 14, 6% at 15, 10% at 16, 15% at 17, 21% at 18 Intelligence, and so on).
 These creatures also have a cumulative chance of 1% per level of experience or Hit Dice of detecting scrying. Treat monsters as the group as which they make saving throws. Check each round of scrying, and if the percentage or less is rolled, the subject 
becomes aware of being watched.
\par \tab A }{\i\fs24 dispel magic}{\fs24  will cause a }{\i\fs24 crystal ball}{\fs24  to cease functioning for one day. The various protections against }{\i\fs24 crystal ball}{\fs24  viewing will simply leave the device hazy and nonfunctioning.
\par \tab You may allow other scrying devices for clerics and druids\emdash water basins and mirrors are suggested. Have them function as normal }{\i\fs24 crystal balls.}{\fs24 
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Crystal Hypnosis Ball:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This cursed item is indistinguishable from a normal }{\i\fs24 crystal ball,}{\fs24  and it radiates magic, but not evil, if detected for. Any wizar
d attempting to use it will become hypnotized, and a telepathic }{\i\fs24 suggestion}{\fs24  will be implanted in his mind.
\par \tab The user of the device will believe that the desired object was viewed, but actually he came partially under the influence of a powerful wizard, lich, or even some power/being from another plane. Each further use brings the }{\i\fs24 crystal ball}{
\fs24  gazer more under the influence of the creature, either as a servant or tool. The DM decides whether to make this a gradual or sudden affair according to the surroundings and circumstances peculiar to the finding of the }{\i\fs24 
crystal hypnosis ball}{\fs24  and the character(s) locating it.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Cube of Force:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This device can be made of ivory, bone, or any hard mineral. It is about the size of a large die\emdash perhaps 3/4 of an inch across\emdash and enables its possessor to put up a }{\i\fs24 
wall of force}{\fs24  10 feet per side around his person. This cubic screen is impervious to the attack forms shown on the table below. The cube has 36 charges, and this energy is restored each day. The holder presses one face of t
he cube to activate or deactivate the field:
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx1440\tx3690\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf6                    Charge Cost Per Turn/\tab \tab \tab 
\par Cube Face\tab Movement Rate\tab Effect}{\fs24\cf6 
\par }{\fs24      1\tab      1/1\tab keeps out gases, wind, etc.\tab 
\par      2\tab      2/8\tab keeps out nonliving matter\tab 
\par      3\tab      3/6\tab keeps out living matter
\par      4\tab      4/4\tab keeps out magic
\par      5\tab      6/3\tab keeps out all things
\par      6\tab      0/normal\tab deactivates
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab When the force screen is up, the following attacks cost extra charges from the cube in order to maintain the integrity of the screen. Note that these spells cannot be cast either into or out of the cube:
