\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Cube of Frost Resistance:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 When the cube is activated it encloses an area 10 feet per side, resembling a }{\i\fs24 cube of force.}{\fs24  The temperat
ure within this area is always 65 degrees F. The field will absorb all cold-based attacks (i.e., }{\i\fs24 cone of cold, ice storm,}{\fs24 
 and even white dragon's breath). However, if the field is subjected to more than 50 points of cold damage in any turn (10 rounds), it 
collapses and cannot be renewed for one hour. If it receives over 100 points of damage in one turn, the cube is destroyed.
\par \tab Cold below 0 degrees F. effectively inflicts 2 points of cold damage on the cube for every -10 degrees F., -4 at -11 to -20, etc. Thus, at -40 degrees F. the device can withstand only 42 points of damage.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Cubic Gate:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 Another small cubic device, this item is fashioned from carnelian. The six sides of the cube are each keyed to a plane, one of which will always be the Prime Material. T
he other five sides/planes can be determined by the DM in any manner he chooses.
\par \tab If a side of the }{\i\fs24 cubic gate}{\fs24  is pressed once, it opens a nexus to the appropriate plane. There is a 10% chance per turn that something will come through it looking for food, fun, or trouble.
\par \tab If a side is pressed twice, the creature so doing, along with all creatures in a 5-foot radius will be drawn through the nexus to the other plane. It is impossible to open more than one nexus at a time.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Daern's Instant Fortress:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This met
al cube is small, but when activated it grows to form a tower 20 feet square and 30 feet high, with arrow slits on all sides and a machicolated battlement atop it. The metal walls extend 10 feet into the ground. The fortress has a small door which will op
en only at the command of the owner of the fortress\emdash even }{\i\fs24 knock}{\fs24  spells can't open the door.
\par \tab The adamantite walls of }{\i\fs24 Daern's instant fortress}{\fs24  are unaffected by normal weapons other than catapults. The tower can absorb 200 points of damage before collapsing. 
Damage sustained is cumulative, and the fortress cannot be repaired (although a }{\i\fs24 wish}{\fs24  will restore 10 points of damage sustained).
\par \tab The fortress springs up in just one round, with the door facing the device's owner. The door will open and close instantly at
 his command. People and creatures (except the owner) must be careful not to be caught by the fortress's sudden growth. Anyone so caught sustains 10d10 points of damage.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Decanter of Endless Water:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This stoppered flask looks ordinary but radiates the aura
 of magic. If the stopper is removed, and the proper words spoken, a stream of fresh or salt water pours out, as ordered. There are separate command words for the amount as well as the type of water. Water can be made to come forth as follows:
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Stream:}{\fs24  pours out 1 gallon per round
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Fountain:}{\fs24  5-foot long stream at 5 gallons per round
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Geyser:}{\fs24  20-foot long stream at 30 gallons per round
\par \tab The geyser causes considerable back pressure, and the holder must be well braced or be knocked over. The force of the geyser will kill small animals and insects (mice, moles, small bats, etc.). The command word must be given to cease.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Deck of Illusions:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This set of parchment cards is usually found in an ivory, leather, or wood box. A full deck consists of 34 cards of 4 suits
. When a card is drawn at random and thrown to the ground, an illusion with audible and visual components is formed. This lasts until dispelled. The illusionary creature will not go more than 30 feet away from where the card landed, but will otherwise mov
e and act as if it were real. When the }{\i\fs24 illusion}{\fs24  is dispelled, the card becomes blank and cannot be used again. If the card is picked up, the }{\i\fs24 illusion}{\fs24 
 is automatically and instantly dispelled. The cards in a deck and the }{\i\fs24 illusions}{\fs24  they bring forth are as follows:
\par 
