\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Girdle of Many Pouches:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This broa
d waistbelt seems to be nothing more than a well-made article of dress. However, if magic is detected for, the item will radiate strong enchantment along with a fainter aura of alteration.
\par \tab Examination will reveal that the girdle has eight small pouches on
 its inner front surface. In fact, there are a total of 64 magical pouches in the girdle, seven others "behind'' each of the eight apparent ones. Each of these pouches is similar to a miniature }{\i\fs24 bag of holding,}{\fs24 
 able to contain up to one cubic foot of materi
al weighing as much as 10 pounds. The girdle responds to the thoughts of its wearer by providing a full pouch (to extract something from) or an empty one (to put something in) as desired. Naturally, this item is greatly prized by spellcasters, for it will
 hold components for many spells and make them readily available.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Gloves of Missile Snaring:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 These gloves radiate slightly of enchantment and alteration if magic is detected for. Once snugly worn, they seem to meld with the hands, becoming almost invisibl
e (undetectable unless within five feet of the wearer). Either or both hands so clad, if not already holding something, can be used to pick many sorts of missiles out of the air, thus preventing possible harm, and enabling the wearer to return a hand-thro
wn missile to its sender as an attack in a subsequent round.
\par \tab All forms of small, hand-hurled or weapon-propelled missiles (arrows, bolts, darts, bullets, javelins, axes, hammers, spears, and the like) can be caught. If the weapon magically returns to the a
ttacker, then catching it simply prevents damage, and returning the weapon does not result in an attack.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Harp of Charming:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This instrument appears identical to all other magical harps. When played by a person proficient in the instrument, the player is able to cast one }{\i\fs24 suggestion}{\fs24 
 spell each turn of playing. Optionally, the DM can require a successful proficiency check be made to cast the }{\i\fs24 suggestion.}{\fs24  On a die roll of 20, the harpist has played so poorly as to enrage all those who hear.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Harp of Discord:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This harp appears normal in all respects. However, when played, the harp emits painful and discordant tones 50% of the time. The remaining 50% of the time it acts as a }{\i\fs24 harp of charming.}{
\fs24  When discordant, the music has the effect of automatically enraging al
l those within 30 feet. Those enraged will attack the musicians 50% of the time or the nearest other target the remaining 50% of the time. The harpist is not affected by this frenzy unless he is being attacked. The frenzy lasts for 1d4 + 1 rounds after th
e music stops.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Hat of Disguise:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This normal-appearing hat contains a powerful enchantment that allows its wearer to alter his appearance as follows:
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx450\adjustright {\fs24 \tab }{\i\fs24 Height:}{\fs24  +/-25% of actual height
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Weight:}{\fs24  +/-50% of actual weight
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Sex:}{\fs24  Male or female
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Hair:}{\fs24  Any color
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Eyes:}{\fs24  Any color
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Complexion:}{\fs24  Any color
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Facial features:}{\fs24  Highly mutable
\par }\pard\plain \s15\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\tab Thus, the wearer could appear as a comely woman, a half-orc, or possibly even a gnome. If the hat is removed, the disguise is instantly dispelled. The headgear can be used over and ove
r. Note that the hat can be changed (as part of a disguise) to appear as a comb, ribbon, head band, fillet, cap, coif, hood, helmet, etc.
\par }\pard\plain \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright \fs20 {\fs24 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Hat of Stupidity:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This hat is indistinguishable from any other magical hat, even when most carefully detected by mag
ical means. Only by placing it upon the head can its powers be determined. Of course, once on the head, the wearer will believe that the hat is a beneficial item, for he will be overcome by stupidity. Intelligence is lowered to 7, or by -1 if the wearer h
as a 7 or lower Intelligence normally. The wearer will always desire to have the hat on\emdash especially when he is engaged in any activity which requires thinking, spellcasting, etc. Without the benefit of a }{\i\fs24 remove curse}{\fs24 
 spell or similar magic, the wearer will never be free from the magic of the hat. If released, the wearer's Intelligence returns to its normal level.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Helm of Brilliance:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 When discovered, a }{\i\fs24 helm of brilliance}{\fs24  appears to be nothing more than an ordinary piece of armor for head protection\emdash a helmet,
 bassinet, mallet, etc. of iron or steel. When worn, it functions only upon the utterance of a special command word. When so empowered the true nature of the helm is visible to all. The helm is armor of +2 value. It is of brilliant silver and polished ste
el, and set with 10 diamonds, 20 rubies, 30 fire opals, and 40 opals\emdash each of large size and magicked\emdash 
which perform as explained below. When struck by bright light, the helm will scintillate and send forth reflective rays in all directions from its crown-like, gem-tipped spikes. The jewels' functions are:
\par 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx1440\adjustright {\fs24 Diamond\tab }{\i\fs24 Prismatic spray}{\fs24  (as the 7th-level wizard spell 
\par Ruby\tab }{\i\fs24 Wall of fire}{\fs24  (as the 5th-level priest spell)
\par Fire Opal \tab }{\i\fs24 Fireball}{\fs24  (as the 3rd-level wizard spell)
\par Opal\tab }{\i\fs24 Light}{\fs24  (as the 1st-level priest spell)
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab Eac
h gem can perform its spell-like power just once. The helm may be used once per round. The level of the spell is doubled to obtain the level at which the spell was cast with respect to range, duration, and such considerations. Until all of its jewels are 
magically expended, a }{\i\fs24 helm of brilliance}{\fs24  also has the following magical properties when activated.
\par \tab 1. It glows with a bluish light when undead are within 30 feet. This light causes pain and 1d6 points of damage to all such creatures except skeletons and zombies.
\par \tab 2. The wearer may command any sword he wields to become a }{\i\fs24 sword of flame.}{\fs24  This is in addition to any other special properties it may have. This takes one round to take effect.
\par \tab 3. The wearer is protected as if a double-strength }{\i\fs24 fire resistance ring}{\fs24  were worn, but this protection cannot be augmented by further magical means.
\par \tab Once all of its jewels have lost their magic, the helm loses all of its powers. The gems turn to worthless powder when this occurs. Removing a jewel destroys the gem. They may not be recharged.
\par \tab If a creature wearing the helm is attacked by magical fire and fails to save vs. magical fire, he 
must attempt another saving throw for the helmet without magical additions. If this is failed, the remaining gems on the helm overload and detonate, inflicting on the wearer whatever accumulated effects the gems would normally have.
\par 
\par }{\fs24\cf6 \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Helm of Comprehending Languages and Reading Magic:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 Appearing as a normal helmet, a }{\i\fs24 helmet of comprehending languages and reading magic}{\fs24 
 enables its wearer to understand 90% of strange tongues and writing
s and 80% of magical writings. (Note that these percentage figures apply to whether all or none of the speaking/writing or inscription is understandable. Understanding does not necessarily imply spell use.) This device is equal to a normal helmet of the t
ype accompanying Armor Class 5.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Helm of Opposite Alignment:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 
This metal hat looks like a typical helmet. If magic is detected for, it radiates magic of an indeterminate sort. Once placed upon the head, however, its curse immediately takes effect, and the alignment of the wearer is radically altered\emdash 
good to evil, neutral to some absolute commitment (LE, LG, CE, CG) as radically different from the former alignment as possible. Alteration in alignment is mental and, once effected, is desired by the individual changed by the magic.
\par \tab Only a }{\i\fs24 wish}{\fs24  can restore former alignment, and the affected individual will not make any attempt to return to the former alignment. If a paladin is concerned, he must undergo a special quest and }{\i\fs24 atone}{\fs24 
 if the curse is to be obliterated. Note that once a }{\i\fs24 helm of opposite alignment}{\fs24  has functioned, it loses all of its magical properties.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Helm of Telepathy:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This sturdy metal helmet appears to be a normal piece of headgear, although it will radiate magic if this is detected for. The wearer of a }{\i\fs24 helm of telepathy}{\fs24 
 is able to determine the thoughts of creatures within a 60-foot range. There are two limitations on this power: The wearer must know the language used by such creatures (the racial tongue will be used in thoughts in preference to th
e Common, the Common in preference to alignment languages); and there can't be more than 3 feet of solid stone, 3 inches of iron, or any solid sheeting of lead or gold between the wearer and the creatures.
\par \tab The thought pick-up is directional. Conscious eff
ort must be made to pick up thoughts. The wearer may communicate by language with any creature within range if there is a mutually known speech, or emotions may be transmitted (empathy) so that a creature will receive the emotional message of the wearer.

\par \tab If the wearer of the helm wants to implant a }{\i\fs24 suggestion}{\fs24  (see the 3rd-level wizard spell of that name in the }{\i\fs24 Player's Handbook}{\fs24 ), he can attempt to do so as follows: The creature receiving the }{\i\fs24 suggestion}{
\fs24  gains a saving throw vs. spell with a -1 penalty for e
very two points of Intelligence lower than the telepathist, but a +1 bonus for every point of Intelligence higher than the wearer of the helm. If Intelligence is equal, no adjustment is made when the saving throw is rolled.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Helm of Teleportation:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This is another helmet of normal appearance which will give off a magical aura if detected for. Any character wearing this device may }{\i\fs24 teleport}{\fs24 
 once per day, exactly as if he were a wizard\emdash the destination must be known, and a risk is involved. If the wearer is a wizard, the helm's full powers can be employed, for the wearer can then memorize a }{\i\fs24 teleportation}{\fs24 
 spell, and use the helm to refresh his memory so he can repeat the spell up to three times upon objects or characters and still be able to personally }{\i\fs24 teleport}{\fs24  by means of the helm. As long as the wizard retains the }{\i\fs24 
teleportation}{\fs24  spell uncast, he can personally }{\i\fs24 teleport}{\fs24  up to six times before the memory of the spell is lost, and even then a usage of the helm remains as noted above for all characters.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Helm of Underwater Action:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 
When this helm is viewed, it is indistinguishable from a normal helmet. However, detection reveals it to be magical, and the possessor is able to see and breathe underwater. Visual properties of the helm are activated when small lenses are 
drawn across the device from compartments on either side. These allow the wearer to see five times farther than water and light conditions allow for normal human vision. (Note that weeds, obstructions, and the like block vision in the usual manner.) If th
e command word is spoken, the }{\i\fs24 helm of underwater action}{\fs24  creates a globe of air around the wearer's head, and maintains it until the command word is spoken again. Thus, the wearer can breathe freely.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Heward's Handy Haversack:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 A magical backpack of this sort appears quite ordinary\emdash 
well-made and well-used. It is of finely tanned leather, and the straps have brass hardware and buckles. There are two side pouches, each of which appears large enough to hold about a quart of material, but each is similar to a }{\i\fs24 bag of holding}{
\fs24  and will actually contain material equal to as much as two cubic feet in volume or 20 pounds in weight. The large central portion of the pack can contain up to eight cubic feet or 80 pounds of material. The pack has an even greater power: When 
the wearer reaches into it for a specific item, that item will always be on top. Thus, no digging around and fumbling is ever necessary to find what the haversack contains. }{\i\fs24 Heward's handy haversack}{\fs24 
 and whatever it contains gain a +2 bonus to all saving throws.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Horn of Blasting:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This magical horn appears to be a normal trumpet, but it radiates magic if a }{\i\fs24 detect magic}{\fs24 
 is cast upon it. It can be sounded as a normal horn, but if the correct word is spoken and the instrument is then played, it has the following effects, both of which happen at once:
\par \tab 1. A cone of sound, 120 feet long and 30 feet wide at the end, issues forth from the horn. All within this area must roll a successful saving throw vs. spell. Those saving are stunned for one round and deafened for
 two. Those failing the saving throw sustain 1d10 points of damage, are stunned for two rounds, and deafened for four.
\par \tab 2. A wave of ultrasonic sound 1 foot wide and 100 feet long issues from the horn. This causes a weakening of such materials as metal, st
one, and wood. The weakening is equal in effect to the damage caused by a hit from a missile hurled by a large catapult. See "Siege Damage" in Chapter 9, and suffer an additional -2 penalty to the die roll described there.
\par \tab If a }{\i\fs24 horn of blasting}{\fs24  is used magically more than once per day, there is a 10% cumulative chance that it will explode and inflict 5d10 points of damage upon the person sounding it.
\par \tab There are no charges upon a horn, but the device is subject to stresses as noted above, and each time it i
s used to magical effect there is a 2% cumulative chance of the instrument self-destructing. In the latter case, no damage is inflicted on the character blowing it.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Horn of Bubbles:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This cursed musical instrument will radiate magic if detected for. It ap
pears as a normal horn, or possibly any of the many magical ones. It will sound a note and call forth a mass of bubbles that completely surround and blind the individual who blew the horn for 2d10 rounds, but these bubbles appear only in the presence of a
 creature actively seeking to slay the character who played the horn, so their appearance might be delayed for a very short or extremely lengthy period.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Horn of Collapsing:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 The horn appears to be a normal musical instrument, perhaps a bugle or warning hor
n of some sort. If it is sounded improperly (e.g., without first speaking the proper command word) or 10% of the time in any event, the following will result:
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Out-of-doors:}{\fs24  A torrent of fist-sized rocks will strike the individual sounding the horn, 2d6 in number, each causing 1d6 hit points of damage.
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Indoors:}{\fs24  The ceiling overhead will collapse when the device is blown. The character suffers 3d12 points of damage.
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Underground:}{\fs24 
 The area immediately above the character sounding the horn will fall upon him. The damage is 5d4 points base, multiplied by one for each 10 feet of height which the material above drops (i.e., twice damage if a 20-foot ceiling, three times damage if a 30
-foot ceiling, etc.).
\par \tab Proper use of a }{\i\fs24 horn of collapsing}{\fs24 
 enables the character to sound it while it is pointed at the roof overhead from 30 to 60 feet beyond the user. The effect is to collapse a section of roof up to 20 feet wide and 20 feet long (10-foot
 radius from the central aiming point) which inflicts damage as noted above if indoors or underground only.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Horn of Fog:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This small, buglelike device allows its possessor to blow forth a thick cloud of heavy fog equal to that of a }{\i\fs24 fog cloud}{\fs24  spell. Each r
ound spent blowing it creates a 10-foot cube fog cloud. The cloud lasts for 2d4 rounds after the last round of blowing the instrument. Note that should it stop being sounded for a round, a new }{\i\fs24 fog cloud}{\fs24 
 will have begun, as the initial one has a life expectancy of but 2d4 more minutes, and will have drifted away from the individual sounding it. The device makes a deep, horn-like noise, the note dropping abruptly to a lower register at the end.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Horn of Goodness/Evil:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This magical instrument adapts itself to
 the alignment of its possessor, so it will produce either a good or an evil effect depending on the alignment of its owner. If the possessor is absolutely neutral, the horn will have no power whatsoever. If the owner is good, then blowing the horn has th
e effect of a }{\i\fs24 protection from evil}{\fs24 
 spell in a 10-foot radius, and this protection will last for 10 rounds. Each friendly/allied creature within this area will be affected as if granted the spell. If the horn is of evil alignment, then the reverse of the not
ed spell occurs within the area of effect. The horn can be blown once per day.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Horn of the Tritons:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This device is a conch shell horn which can be blown once per day (except by a triton who can sound it three times daily). A }{\i\fs24 horn of the tritons}{\fs24  can do an
y one of the following functions when blown:
\par \tab 1. Calm rough waters in a one mile radius. (This has the effect of dispelling a water elemental or water weird.)
\par \tab 2. Summon 5d4 hippocampi (on a d6 roll of 1 or 2), 5d6 giant sea horses (on a roll of 3-5), or 1
d10 sea lions (on a roll of 6) if the character is in a body of water in which such creatures dwell. The creatures summoned will be friendly and will obey, to the best of their understanding, the character who sounded the horn.
\par \tab 3. Panic marine creatures with animal or lower Intelligence, causing them to flee unless each saves vs. spell. Those who do save must take a -5 penalty on their attack rolls for 3d6 turns (30-180 rounds).
\par \tab Any sounding of a }{\i\fs24 horn of the tritons}{\fs24  can be heard by all tritons within a three-mile radius.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Horn of Valhalla:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 
There are four varieties of this magical device. Each appears to be a normal instrument until its command word is spoken. Then, each summons a number of berserkers from Valhalla to fight for the character who summoned t
hem by blowing the horn. Each variety of horn can be blown just once every seven days. The type of horn, its powers, and who is able to employ it are determined by rolling 1d20 and consulting the table below.
\par \tab Any character whose group is unable to employ a particular }{\i\fs24 horn of Valhalla}{\fs24  will be attacked by the berserk fighters summoned when the character blows the horn.
\par \tab Summoned fighters are Armor Class 4, have 6 hp points per die, and are armed with sword and spear (50%), or battle-axe and spear (50%). They
 gladly attack anyone the possessor of the horn commands them to fight, until they or their opponents are slain, or six turns have elapsed, whichever occurs first.
\par \tab Fully 50% of these horns are aligned and will summon only fighters of the horn's alignment. A radical alignment difference will cause the horn blower to be attacked by the fighters.
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx1440\tx3600\tx5760\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf6 \tab \tab Berserk Fighters\tab 
\par D20 Roll\tab Type of Horn\tab     Summoned\tab Usable By}{\fs24\cf6 
\par }{\fs24 1-8\tab     Silver\tab 2d4+2  2nd level\tab any group
\par 9-15\tab     Brass\tab 2d4+1 3rd level\tab P, Wi, R
\par 16-18\tab     Bronze\tab 2d4 4th level\tab P, Wa
\par 19-20\tab     Iron\tab 1d4+1 5th level\tab Wa
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Horseshoes of Speed:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 These iron shoes come in sets of four like ordinary horseshoes, but they are magical and will not wear out. When affixed to a horse's hooves, they double the animal's speed. There
 is a 1% chance per 20 miles traveled that a shoe will drop off, and if this passes unnoticed, the horse's speed will drop to 150% normal rate. If two or more are lost, speed returns to normal.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Horseshoes of a Zephyr:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 These iron shoes can be affixed like normal horseshoes, but they allow a horse to travel without actually touching the ground. Among other things, this means water can be crossed\emdash 
passed over without effort\emdash and movement is possible without leaving tracks on
 any sort of ground. The horse is able to move at normal speeds, and it will not tire for as long as 12 hours' continuous riding per day when wearing these magical horseshoes.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Incense of Meditation:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 The small rectangular blocks of sweet-smelling }{\i\fs24 incense of meditation}{\fs24 
 are indistinguishable from nonmagical incense until one is lit. When burning, the special fragrance and pearly-hued smoke of this special incense are recognizable by any priest of 5th or higher level.
\par \tab When a priest lights a block of the incense of meditation and spends eight hours praying and meditating nearby, the incense will enable him to gain maximum spell effects. Thus, }{\i\fs24 cure wounds}{\fs24 
 spells are always maximum, spell effects are of the broadest area possible, and saving throws against their effects suffer -1 penalties, and when dead are brought back to life, their chance of not surviving is reduced by one-half (rounded down).
\par \tab When this item of magic is discovered, there will be 2d4 pieces of incense. Each piece burns for eight hours, the effects remain for 24 hours.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Incense of Obsession:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 These strange blocks of incense exactly resemble }{\i\fs24 incense of meditation.}{\fs24  If meditation and prayer are conducted while the lit }{\i\fs24 incense of obsession}{\fs24 
 is nearby, its odor and smoke will cause the priest to beco
me totally confident that his spell ability is superior, due to the magical incense. The priest will be determined to use his spells at every opportunity, even when not needed or when useless. The priest will remain obsessed with his abilities and spells 
until all are cast or 24 hours have elapsed.
\par \tab There are 2d4 pieces of this incense normally, each burning for one hour.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Ioun Stones:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 These magical stones always float in the air and must be within 3 feet of their owner to be of any use. When a character f
irst acquires the stones, he must hold each and then release it, so it takes up a circling orbit, whirling and trailing, circling 1d3 feet from his head. Thereafter, the stones must be grasped or netted to separate them their owner. The owner may voluntar
i
ly seize and stow the stones (at night, for example) to keep them safe, but he loses the benefits of the stones during that time. 1d10 ioun stones will be found, though there are 14 different kinds, in all. Roll 1d20 to determine the property of each ston
e, a duplication indicating a stone which is burned out and useless but counts as one of the number found:
\par \tab Whenever ioun stones are exposed to attack, they are treated as Armor Class -4 and take 10 points of damage to destroy. They save as if they were of hard metal\emdash +3 bonus.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs36\cf6 IOUN STONES}{\fs36\cf6 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx1080\tx3150\tx4590\adjustright {\b\fs24 D20\tab Color of
