\par    }{\b\fs24\cf6 Bow +1:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 
This gives a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls to arrows fired from it. If magical arrows are used, total the bonuses of both the bow and the arrows used. The type of bow found (composite, short, long, etc.) should be based on the circumstances of your 
campaign and the nature of the area. A nonmagical arrow fired from a magical bow is a nonmagical missile.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Crossbow of Accuracy, +3:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This gives a +3 bonus to attack rolls with its missiles but not to damage. All ranges are considered short. About 10% of these weapons will be heavy crossbows.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Crossbow of Distance:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This has double range in all categories. About 10% of these weapons will be heavy crossbows. This weapon is otherwise +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Crossbow of Speed:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This item allows its possessor to double the rate of fire normal for the weapon. If it is grasped, the }{\i\fs24 crossbow of speed}{\fs24 
 will automatically cock itself. In surprise situations it is of no help. Otherwise, it allows first fire in any melee round, and end-of-round fire also, w
hen applicable. About 10% of these weapons are heavy crossbows. The weapon has a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Dagger +2, Longtooth:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This appears to be a normal weapon, or perhaps a nonspecial magical weapon. However, when this broad-bladed weapon
 is wielded by a small demihuman (like a gnome or halfling), it will actually lengthen and function as a short sword (retaining its +2 bonus in this form). Even when functioning in this way it remains as light and handy to use as a dagger would be in the 
hands of the same character. The weapon will actually penetrate wood or stone as easily as it will softer material, inflicting maximum damage against either substance.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Dagger of Throwing:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This appears to be a normal weapon but will radiate strongly of mag
ic when this is checked for. The balance of this sturdy blade is perfect, such that when it is thrown by anyone, the dagger will demonstrate superb characteristics as a ranged weapon. The magic of the dagger enables it to be hurled up to 180 feet. A succe
ssful hit when it is thrown will inflict twice normal dagger damage, plus the bonus provided by the blade, which will range from +1 to +4. To determine the bonus for a specific dagger, roll percentile dice and consult the following table:
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s7\keep\keepn\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx1440\tx2880\outlinelevel6\adjustright \b\cf6 {\tab Magical\tab 
\par }\pard\plain \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx1440\tx2880\adjustright \fs20 {\b\fs24\cf6 D100 Roll\tab Bonus\tab XP Value}{\fs24\cf6 \tab 
\par }{\fs24 01-35\tab +1\tab 250\tab 
\par 36-65\tab +2\tab 350\tab 
\par 66-90\tab +3\tab 450\tab 
\par 91-00\tab +4\tab 550\tab 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Dagger of Venom:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This appears to be a standard }{\i\fs24 dagger +1,}{\fs24  but its hilt holds a hidden store of poison. Any hit on a roll of 20 injects fatal poison into the opponent unless a savi
ng throw vs. poison is successful. The }{\i\fs24 dagger of venom}{\fs24  holds up to six doses of poison. If the hilt contains fewer than six doses, the owner can pour more in up to the maximum. (Use of this weapon by good\emdash particularly lawful good
\emdash characters must be carefully monitored for effects on alignment.)
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Darts of Homing:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 These appear to be normal projectiles, but are actually +3 magical weapons. If a dart hits the intended target, it will magically return to the thrower in the same round and can be re-used. A dart 
inflicts a base 1d6 points of damage plus its magical bonus on a successful hit against any size creature (4-9 points total). A dart that misses its target loses its magical power. These weapons have twice the range of ordinary darts\emdash 
20 yards short, 40 yards medium, 80 yards long.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Hammer +3, Dwarven Thrower:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This appears to be a standard }{\i\fs24 hammer +2.}{\fs24 
 In the hands of a dwarven fighter who knows the appropriate command word, its full potential is realized. In addition to the +3 bonus, the hammer has the following characteristics:
\par \tab The hammer has a 180-foot range and will return to its wielder's hand like a boomerang. It has a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls. When hurled, the hammer inflicts double damage against all opponents except giants (including ogres
, ogre magi, trolls, and ettins).  Against giants it causes triple damage (plus the bonus of +3).
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Hammer of Thunderbolts:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 
This appears to be a large, extra-heavy hammer. A character less than 6 feet tall and with Strength less than 18/01 will find it too unbalanced to wield properly in combat. However, a character of sufficient Strength and size will find that the hammer fun
ctions with a +3 bonus and gains double damage dice on any hit.
\par \tab If the wielder wears a }{\i\fs24 girdle of giant strength}{\fs24  and }{\i\fs24 gauntlets of ogre power}{\fs24  and he knows the hammer's true name, the weapon can be used to full effect: When swung or hurled it gains a +5 bonus
, double damage dice, all }{\i\fs24 girdle}{\fs24  and }{\i\fs24 gauntlet}{\fs24  bonuses, and it strikes dead any giant upon which it scores a hit.
\par \tab (Depending on the campaign, the DM might wish to limit the effect to exclude storm giants and include ogres, ogre magi, trolls, ettins, and clay, flesh, and stone golems.)
\par \tab When hurled and successfully hitting, a great noise, like a clap of thunder, stuns all creatures within 90 feet for one round. Throwing range is 180 feet. (Thor would throw the hammer about double the above range.) The }{\i\fs24 hammer
 of thunderbolts}{\fs24  is difficult to hurl, so only one throw every other round can be made. After five throws within the space of any two-turn period, the wielder must rest for one turn.
\par \tab Hammers can be hurled as hand axes.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Hornblade:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This is a magical weapon with a sickle-like blade resembling some sort of animal horn. }{\i\fs24 Hornblades}{\fs24 
 range in size from that of a knife to somewhat less than the length of a short sword. Even a close inspection is 90% unlikely to reveal it as anything other than a piece of horn of a \'bd-foot to 1\'bc
-foot in length, set in some sort of handle or grip. If magic is detected for, a }{\i\fs24 hornblade}{\fs24 
 will radiate faintly of enchantment magic. However, if the proper pressure is applied in the correct place, a curved blade of great strength and sharpness will spring out.
\par \tab The small versions (knife-sized and dagger-sized) are usually enchanted to +1 or +2, and the largest version (scimitar-sized) commonly has a bonus of +2 or +3. Smaller }{\i\fs24 hornblades}{\fs24 
 can be thrown, and the bonus applies to both the attack number and damage determination.
\par \tab Any character class permitted to use sickle-like weapons can use a }{\i\fs24 hornblade.}{\fs24  The possessor can use it with proficiency, providing he has proficiency with the appropriately sized weapon (knife, dagger, or scimitar).
\par \tab The experience-point value of a }{\i\fs24 hornblade}{\fs24  depends upon its size and the amount of its magical bonus:
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s7\keep\keepn\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx2160\outlinelevel6\adjustright \b\cf6 {Size\tab XP Value\tab 
\par }\pard\plain \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx2160\adjustright \fs20 {\fs24 Knife-sized\tab 500 per "plus"\tab 
\par Dagger-sized\tab 750 per "plus"\tab 
\par Scimitar-sized\tab 1,000 per "plus"\tab 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Javelin of Lightning:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 A }{\i\fs24 javelin of lightning}{\fs24  is con
sidered equal to a +2 magical weapon, although it has neither attack nor damage bonuses. It has a range of 90 yards and whenever it strikes, the javelin becomes the head of a 5-foot wide, 30-foot long stroke of lightning. Any creature hit by the javelin s
uffers 1d6 points of damage, plus 20 points of electrical damage. Any other creatures in the path of the stroke take either 10 or 20 points of damage, based on whether their saving throws are successful or not.
\par \tab From 2-5 javelins will be found. The javelin is consumed in the lightning discharge.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Javelin of Piercing:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This weapon is not actually hurled\emdash when a command word is spoken, the }{\i\fs24 javelin of piercing}{\fs24 
 launches itself. Range is 180 feet, all distances considered as short range. The javelin has a +6 bonus
 to attack rolls and inflicts 1d6+6 points of damage. (Note this missile will fly horizontally, vertically, or any combination thereof to the full extent of its range.) From 2-8 (2d4) will be found at one time. The magic of the }{\i\fs24 
javelin of piercing}{\fs24  is good for only one throw after which it becomes a normal javelin.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Knife, Buckle:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This magical blade has a hilt that looks just like a large belt-buckle ornament or a complete small buckle. The hilt can be grasped easily and the weapon drawn from its belt-sheat
h. The knife blade is short but has a very sharp point\emdash it inflicts damage as a knife.
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx1440\tx2160\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf6 D10 Roll\tab Type\tab XP Value\tab 
\par }{\fs24 1-4\tab +1\tab 100\tab 
\par 5-7\tab +2\tab 200\tab 
\par 8-9\tab +3\tab 300\tab 
\par 10\tab +4\tab 400\tab 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Mace of Disruption:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This appears to be a }{\i\fs24 mace +1,}{\fs24  but it has a neutral good align
ment, and any evil character touching it will receive 5d4 points of damage due to the powerful enchantments laid upon the weapon. If a }{\i\fs24 mace of disruption}{\fs24 
 strikes any undead creature or evil creature from one of the lower planes, may utterly destroy the creature.
\par \tab Skeletons, zombies, ghouls, shadows, wights, and ghasts, if hit, are instantly blasted out of existence. Other creatures roll saving throws as follows:
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx3240\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf6 Creature\tab Save}{\fs24\cf6 \tab 
\par }{\fs24 Wraiths\tab   5%\tab 
\par Mummies\tab 20%\tab 
\par Spectres\tab 35%\tab 
\par Vampires\tab 50%\tab 
\par Ghosts\tab 65%\tab 
\par Liches\tab 80%\tab 
\par Other affected evil creatures\tab 95%\tab 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab Even if these saving throws are effective, the }{\i\fs24 mace of disruption}{\fs24  scores double damage upon opponents of this sort, and twice the damage bonus.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Net of Entrapment:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This magical rope net is strong enough to defy Strength
 under 20 and is equal to AC -10 with respect to blows aimed at cutting it. (Normal sawing attempts to cut it with dagger or sword will not succeed; to sever a strand of the mesh, a character must hack at it until he does 5 points of damage on a strand.)

\par \tab 
Each net is 10 feet square and has a 3-inch-square mesh. It can be thrown 20 feet so as to cover and close upon opponents; each creature in range must roll a successful saving throw vs. dragon breath to avoid being entrapped. It can be suspended from a ce
iling (or generally overhead) and drop upon a command word. It can be laid upon the floor and close upward upon command. The net stretches so as to close over an area up to five cubic feet. It can be loosened by its possessor on command.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Net of Snaring:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This net looks just like a }{\i\fs24 net of entrapment,}{\fs24 
 but it functions only underwater. There, it can be commanded to shoot forth up to 30 feet to trap a creature. It is otherwise the same as the }{\i\fs24 net of entrapment.}{\fs24 
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Quarterstaff, Magical:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This appears to be a norm
al bronzewood staff banded with iron. The shaft is actually as strong as steel, and has two magical qualities. Upon command, the staff will alter its length from as short as 6 feet to as long as 12 feet (or any length in between). It inflicts damage as a 
quarterstaff (base amount, 1d6 points), with additions to attack and damage rolls based upon its magical bonus.
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx1440\tx2880\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf6 D20 Roll\tab Type\tab XP Value
\par }{\fs24  1-5\tab +1\tab    250\tab 
\par  6-9\tab +2\tab    500\tab 
\par 10-13\tab +3\tab    750\tab 
\par 14-17\tab +4\tab 1,000\tab 
\par 18-20\tab +5\tab 1,250\tab 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 
\par }{\b\fs24 \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Scimitar of Speed:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This is a magical w
eapon, usually of +2 bonus, that automatically grants its wielder the first attack in a melee round, even though some magical effect might have otherwise slowed his speed and reaction time. It also allows more than one strike in some rounds, increasing th
e wielder's figure for attacks per melee round by one place, so that if one attack is normal, then the improvement is to two attacks per round. This increase in attacks is cumulative with any other bonus attacks (such as those provided by a }{\i\fs24 
haste}{\fs24  spell).
\par \tab The order of attacks in the round is determined normally after the wielder of the }{\i\fs24 scimitar of speed}{\fs24 
 has made his first attack to begin activity in the round. It is possible, for instance, that a wielder entitled to three attacks in the round will attack onc
e before any other action takes place, and then (because of poor initiative rolls or other factors) take his remaining two attacks at the very end of the round.
\par \tab There is a chance (25%) that the weapon will have a bonus of something other than +2; if this occurs, roll percentile dice and refer to the following table to determine the appropriate bonus:
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s7\keep\keepn\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx2160\tx3600\outlinelevel6\adjustright \b\cf6 {D100 Roll\tab Type\tab XP Value\tab 
\par }\pard\plain \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx2160\tx3600\adjustright \fs20 {\fs24 01-50\tab +1\tab 2,500\tab 
\par (normal form)\tab +2\tab 3,000\tab 
\par 51-75\tab +3\tab 3,500\tab 
\par 76-90\tab +4\tab 4,000\tab 
\par 91-00\tab +5\tab 4,500\tab 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sling of Seeking +2:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This gives its user a
 +2 bonus for both attack and damage rolls, but missiles from such a weapon are regarded as +1 with respect to whether or not certain creatures are affected by the weapon (i.e., a special defense of "+1 or better weapon to hit" means the creature is vulne
rable to normal missiles from this sling).
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Spear, Cursed Backbiter:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This is to all tests a magical spear with a +1 bonus (or at the DM's option +2 or +3). It may even function normally in combat against a deadly enemy, but each time it is used in melee ag
ainst a foe, there is a one in 20 cumulative chance that it will function against its wielder. Once it begins functioning in this way, you can't get rid of it without a }{\i\fs24 remove curse}{\fs24 
 spell. The character always seems to find the spear in his hand despite his best efforts or intentions.
\par \tab When the curse takes effect, the spear curls around to strike its wielder in the back, negating any shield and Dexterity bonuses to Armor Class, and inflicting normal damage. The curse even functions when the spear is hurled,
 but if the wielder has hurled the spear, the damage done to the hurler will be double. Once the spear has returned to him, the character will again find himself compelled to use the spear.
\par 
\par }{\b\fs24 \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sun Blade:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This sword is the size of a bastard sword. However, its enchantment enables the }{\i\fs24 sun blade}{\fs24 
 to be wielded as if it were a short sword with respect to encumbrance, weight, speed factor, and ease of use (i.e., the weapon appears to all viewers to be a bastard sword, and inflicts bastard sword damage, but the wie
lder feels and reacts as if the weapon were a short sword). Any individual able to use either a bastard sword or a short sword with proficiency is proficient in the use of a }{\i\fs24 sun blade.}{\fs24 
\par \tab In normal combat, the glowing golden blade of the weapon is equal to a
 +2 sword. Against evil creatures, its bonus is +4. Against Negative Energy Plane creatures or those drawing power from that plane (such as certain undead), the sword inflicts double damage.
\par \tab Furthermore, the blade has a special }{\i\fs24 sunray}{\fs24  power. Once a day, u
pon command, the blade can be swung vigorously above the head, and it will shed a bright yellow radiance that is like full daylight. The radiance begins shining in a 10-foot radius around the sword-wielder, spreading outward at 5 feet per round for 10 rou
nds thereafter, creating a globe of light with a 60-foot radius. When the swinging stops, the radiance fades to a dim glow that persists for another turn before disappearing entirely. All }{\i\fs24 sun blades}{\fs24  are of good alignment.
\par 
\par }{\fs24\cf6 \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sword +1, +2 vs. magic-using and enchanted creatures:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 
This sword always provides a +1 bonus. The +2 bonus takes effect when the sword is employed against wizards, monsters that can cast spells, and conjured, created, gated, or summoned creatures. Note that the +2 bonus would not operate a
gainst a creature magically empowered by an item (such as a }{\i\fs24 ring of spell storing}{\fs24 ) to cast spells.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sword +1, +3 vs. lycanthropes and shape changers:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This gives its +3 against werecreatures\emdash those able to assume the form of another creature (such as a vamp
ire or a druid), or any creature under the influence of a }{\i\fs24 polymorph}{\fs24  or }{\i\fs24 shape change}{\fs24  spell.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sword +1, +3 vs. regenerating creatures:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This will give the +3 bonus to its wielder even when the regenerating creature does so because of a magical device\emdash such as a }{\i\fs24 ring of regeneration.}{\fs24 

\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sword +1, +4 vs. reptiles:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 this gives the +4 against such creatures as dinosaurs, dragons, hydras, lizards, snakes, wyverns, etc.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sword +1, cursed:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This performs in all respects as a +1 weapon, but when its wielder is faced by 
an enemy, the sword will weld itself to the character's hand and force him to fight until the enemy or the wielder is slain. Thereafter, the possessor can loose, but never rid himself of, the cursed sword. No matter what is done, it will appear in his han
d whenever an opponent is faced. The character can be freed of the weapon only by a }{\i\fs24 remove curse}{\fs24  spell.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sword +1, flame tongue, +2 vs. regenerating creatures, +3 vs. cold-using, inflammable, or avian creatures, +4 vs. undead:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This sheds light when its possessor speaks a command word or phrase. When activated, the }{
\i\fs24 flame tongue}{\fs24  sword's fire illuminates the area as brightly as a torch. The flame from this sword easily ignites oil, burns webs, or sets fire to paper, parchment, dry wood, etc. Cold-using creatur
es are those whose attack mode involves cold (ice toads, white dragons, winter wolves, yeti, etc.).
\par 
\par }{\fs24\cf6 \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sword +1, Luck Blade:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This gives its possessor a +1 bonus to all saving throws and will have 1d4+1 }{\i\fs24 wishes.}{\fs24  The DM should keep the number of wishes secret.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sword +2, Dragon Slayer:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 
This has a +4 bonus against any sort of true dragon. It inflicts triple damage against one sort of dragon (i.e., 3d12+4). Note that an unusual sword with intelligence and alignment will not be made to slay dragons of the same al
ignment. Determine dragon type (excluding unique ones like Bahamut and Tiamat) by rolling 1d10:
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx180\tx2880\adjustright {\fs24 \tab 1 black (CE)\tab   6 gold (LG)
\par }\pard\plain \s15\keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx180\tx2880\adjustright {\tab 2 blue (LE)\tab     7 green (LE)
\par }\pard\plain \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx180\tx2880\adjustright \fs20 {\fs24 \tab 3 brass (CG)\tab   8 red (CE)
\par \tab 4 bronze (LG)\tab   9 silver (LG)
\par \tab 5 copper (CG)\tab 10 white (CE)
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sword +2, Giant Slayer:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 
This provides a +3 bonus versus any giant, giant-kin, ettin, ogre mage, or titan. Against any of the true giants (hill, stone, frost, fire, cloud, storm) the sword causes double damage (i.e., 2d12+3).
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sword, Short, of Quickness:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This is a special +2 blade that enables the wielder to strike first in every combat round. If the wielder encounters someone with a similar weapon (e.g., a }{\i\fs24 scimitar of speed}{
\fs24 ), both strike simultaneously.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sword+2, Nine Lives Stealer:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This will always perf
orm as a +2 weapon, but it also has the power to draw the life force from an opponent. It can do this nine times before the ability is lost. A natural 20 must be scored on the wielder's attack roll for the sword to function. The victim is entitled to a sa
ving throw vs. spell. If this succeeds, the sword does not function, no charge is used, and normal damage is determined.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sword+3, Frost Brand, +6 vs. fire-using/dwelling creatures:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This sword always provides a +3 bonus. The +6 bonus takes effect against c
reatures that use fire or live in fiery environments. The weapon does not shed any light, except when the air temperature is below 0 degrees F. It does give special benefits against fire, for its wielder is protected as if he were wearing a }{\i\fs24 
ring of fire resistance.}{\fs24 
\par \tab The }{\i\fs24 frost brand}{\fs24  sword also has a 50% chance of extinguishing any fire into which its blade is thrust. This power extends to a 10-foot radius\emdash including a }{\i\fs24 wall of fire}{\fs24  but excluding a }{\i\fs24 
fireball, meteor swarm,}{\fs24  or }{\i\fs24 flame strike.}{\fs24 
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sword,+4 Defender:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 T
his gives its wielder the option of using all, some, or none of the +4 bonus in defense (improving his Armor Class) against any opponent using a hand-held weapon, such as a dagger, mace, spear (not hurled), sword, etc. For example, the wielder can, on the
 first round of battle, opt to use the sword as +2 and save the other two bonus factors to be added to his Armor Class. This can be done each round.
\par \tab Note that there is also a }{\i\fs24 sword, +5 defender.}{\fs24  This is identical to the +4 sword with one extra bonus point.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sword, +5 Holy Avenger:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 In the hands of any character other than a paladin, this holy sword will perform only as a }{\i\fs24 sword +2.}{\fs24 
 In the hands of a paladin, however, it creates a magic resistance of 50% in a 5-foot radius, dispels magic in a 5-foot radius at the level of the paladin, and inflicts +10 points of bonus damage upon chaotic evil opponents.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sword -2, cursed:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This is a sword that gives off a magical aura and performs well against targets in practice, but when it is used against an opponent in comb
at it lowers its user's attack rolls by -2. Only by careful observation can this lowering be detected.
\par \tab All damage scored is reduced by 2 hit points, but never below a 1 in any event. The sword will always force the character to employ it against enemies, appearing in the character's hand. It can be gotten rid of only by means of }{\i\fs24 limited wish
}{\fs24  or }{\i\fs24 wish.}{\fs24 
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sword of Dancing:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 On the first round of melee this weapon is +1, on the second +2, on the third +3, and on the fourth it is +4. On the fifth round, it drops
 back to +1 and the cycle begins again. In addition, after four rounds of melee its wielder can opt to allow it to "dance."
\par \tab Dancing consists of loosing the sword on any round (after the first) when its bonus is +1. The sword then fights on its own at the 
same level of experience as its wielder. After four rounds of dancing, the sword returns to its wielder, who must hold it (and use it) for four rounds before it can dance again. In other words, it is loosed to dance for four more rounds, going from +1 to 
+4, and must then be held by its wielder at a +1 state and physically used for four successive rounds of melee combat.
\par \tab When dancing, the sword will leave its owner's hand and may go up to 30 feet distant. At the end of its fourth round of solo combat, it w
ill move to its possessor's hand automatically. Note that when dancing the sword cannot be physically hit, although certain magical attacks such as a }{\i\fs24 fireball, lightning bolt,}{\fs24  or }{\i\fs24 transmute metal to wood}{\fs24 
 spell could affect it.
\par \tab Finally, remember that the }{\i\fs24 dancing sword}{\fs24 
 fights alone exactly the same; if a 7th-level thief is the wielder, the sword will so fight when dancing. Relieved of his weapon for four melee rounds, the possessor may act in virtually any manner desired\emdash resting, discharging missiles, drawing
 another weapon and engaging in hand-to-hand combat, etc.\emdash as long as he remains within 30 feet of the sword. If he moves more than 30 feet from the weapon, it falls lifeless to the ground and is a +1 weapon when again grasped.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sword of Wounding:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This is a sword of only +1 bonus, but any hit made with it cannot be healed by }{\i\fs24 regeneration.}{\fs24 
 In subsequent rounds, the opponent so wounded loses one additional hit point for each wound inflicted by the sword.
\par \tab Thus, an opponent hit for four points of damage on the
 first melee round will automatically lose one additional hit point on the second and each successive round of combat. Loss of the extra point stops only when the creature so wounded bandages its wound or after 10 melee rounds (one turn).
\par \tab Damage from a }{\i\fs24 sword of wounding}{\fs24  can be healed only by normal means (rest and time), never by potion, spell, or other magical means short of a }{\i\fs24 wish.}{\fs24 
 Note that successive wounds will damage in the same manner as the first.
\par 
\par }{\fs24\cf6 \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sword of Life Stealing:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This +2 weapon will elimi
nate one level of experience (or Hit Die) and accompanying hit points and abilities when it strikes any opponent on a natural roll of 20. This function is the same as the level-draining ability of certain undead creatures.
\par \tab The sword wielder can gain as ma
ny hit points as an opponent loses to this function of the weapon, up to the maximum number of hit points the character is allowed (i.e., only a character who has suffered loss of hit points can benefit from the function).
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sword of Sharpness:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 
This weapon is treated as +3 or better for purposes of who or what can be hit by it, even though it gets only a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls. Its power is great, however, for on a very high attack roll, it will sever an extremity\emdash 
arm, leg, neck, tail, tentacle, whatever (but not head) determined by random dice roll:
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s7\keep\keepn\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx2880\outlinelevel6\adjustright \b\cf6 {\tab \tab Modified score
\par }\pard\plain \keep\nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx2880\adjustright \fs20 {\b\fs24\cf6 Opponent is\tab to sever*}{\fs24\cf6 
\par }{\fs24 normal/armored\tab 19-21
\par larger than man-sized\tab 20-21
\par Solid metal or stone\tab 21
\par * Considering only the sword's bonus of +1.
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx-720\tx240\tx480\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab A }{\i\fs24 sword of sharpness}{\fs24  will respond to its wielder's desire with respect to the light it sheds\emdash none, a 5-foot circle of dim illumination, a 15-foot light, or a 30-foot radius glow equal to a }{\i\fs24 light}{\fs24  spell.

\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sword, Vorpal:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 Similar but superior to a }{\i\fs24 sword of sharpness,}{\fs24  a }{\i\fs24 vorpal}{\fs24  weapon has
 a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls. Check the table below to determine whether an attack roll is good enough to sever the neck/head of the opponent:
\par 
