\par \tab Note that many creatures have no heads or can change their form and, therefore, cannot suffer decapitation. There are also creatures that have heads but will not necessarily be killed by decapitati
on (among these are dopplegangers, elementals, and golems).
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sword of the Planes:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This magical weapon has a base bonus of +1 on the Pr
ime Material Plane, but on any Inner Plane its bonus increases to +2. (The +2 bonus also applies on the Prime Material Plane when the weapon is used against }{\i\fs24 opponents}{\fs24 
 from the Inner Planes.) Similarly, when used on an Outer Plane or against creatures from 
the Outer Planes, the sword becomes a +3 weapon. Finally, it operates as a +4 weapon on the Astral or Ethereal Plane or when used against opponents from either of those planes.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Sword, Cursed Berserking:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 This performs by every test, save that of the heat 
of battle, as a +2 magical sword of some sort. However, in actual battle its wielder will go berserk, attacking the nearest creature and continuing to fight until dead or until no living thing remains within 60 feet. The sword has a +2 bonus and otherwise
 acts as a }{\i\fs24 cursed sword +1.}{\fs24  The possessor of a }{\i\fs24 cursed berserking sword}{\fs24  can be rid of it only if it is exorcised via a }{\i\fs24 remove curse}{\fs24  spell or }{\i\fs24 wish.}{\fs24 
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Trident of Submission:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 A weapon of this nature appears unremarkable, exactly as any normal trident. The wielder of a }{\i\fs24 trident of submission}{\fs24 
 causes any opponent struck to save vs. spell. If the opponent fails to save, it must check morale the next round }{\i\fs24 instead}{\fs24  of attacking; if morale is good, the opponent may act normally next round, but if it is poor, the opponen
t will cease fighting and surrender, overcome with a feeling of hopelessness. The duration of this hopelessness is 2-8 rounds. Thereafter the creature is normal once again. The trident has 17-20 charges. A trident of this type is a +1 magical weapon.

\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Trident of Fish Command:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 
This three-tined fork atop a stout 6-foot long rod appears to be a barbed military fork of some sort. However, its magical properties enable its wielder to cause all fish within a 60-foot radius to roll saving throws vs. spell. This u
ses one charge of the trident. Fish failing this throw are completely under empathic command and will not attack the possessor of the trident nor any creature within 10 feet of him. The wielder of the device can cause fish to move in whatever direction is
 desired and can convey messages of emotion (i.e., fear, hunger, anger, indifference, repletion, etc.). Fish making their saving throw are free of empathic control, but they will not approach within 10 feet of the trident.
\par \tab In addition to ordinary fish, the trident affects sharks and eels. It doesn't affect mollusks, crustaceans, amphibians, reptiles, mammals, and similar sorts of nonpiscine marine creatures. A school of fish should be checked as a single entity.
\par \tab A trident of this type contains 1d4+16 charges. It is otherwise a +1 magical weapon.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Trident of Warning:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 A weapon of this type enables its wielder to determine the location, depth, species, and number of hostile or hungry marine predators within 240 feet. A }{\i\fs24 trident of warning}{\fs24 
 must be grasped and p
ointed in order for the person using it to gain such information, and it requires one round to scan a hemisphere with a radius of 240 feet. There are 19-24 charges in a trident of this type, each charge sufficient to last for two rounds of scanning. The w
eapon is otherwise a +2 magical weapon.
\par 
\par \tab }{\b\fs24\cf6 Trident of Yearning:}{\fs24\cf6  }{\fs24 A }{\i\fs24 trident of yearning}{\fs24 
 looks exactly like any normal trident, and its aura is indistinguishable from that of other enchanted weapons of this sort. Any character grasping this type of trident imme
diately feels an overwhelming desire to immerse himself in as great a depth of water as possible. This unquenchable longing causes the affected character to proceed immediately toward the largest/deepest body of water\emdash 
in any event, one that is sufficient to completely cover his or her person. Once there, he will immerse himself permanently.
\par \tab The character cannot loose his grip on the trident, and only a }{\i\fs24 water breathing}{\fs24  spell (after submersion) or a }{\i\fs24 wish}{\fs24  will enable the character to do so. The trident is oth
erwise a -2 cursed magical weapon. Note that this item does not confer the ability to breathe underwater.
\par 
\par 
